mlQE3d0-9YFqTHQxwRk9raaTb834EODHdACfYwLOccKrwmahmRCapgSkxQjbODqFVkSjZZodwgndfR-NA6Im6_dZG4pu-8wVjwZnbQgu-9OcKM9qsAZMdW5n8Uvn-mZk1w65StCw9BJ0nsqNj82osLEb0Vp1HmI851Ey-AQfoTpr2RTvKFCc3v0pE6X60g0GqRcknzs8zAI0Xt7GSyO5rRJW5V3A0Y0bMCUYrRigl16LWNoE40e6I_bwKc5hf5fpK7IyJBTUolRBMR182rg9Opgr8Q7Zr5Y_Tt_IaXg48S08ZSMUBKYy6Gqgb2C5xTLBfO3N3s9gRHjzVG9g73sQW0kXGxFMKO6-iZhZ8KXBR-j6HWs0qinNZjJTp4gqXcrxejKKoGYY_91Sn_GKhy-dJtfLtcDYQqp7dXXmtLG96xx9BgRhNnQFoWg2NLvcafxJ5LjbHJ_5Rzl6vMc8Db2nVy0IO_iNbXq0Db6r9wcutS2lXa85NnprZsb1x-E0nFcFGC0lTklNNi1Tb6RNrtFlRx3VcA1e0kyBUW864U1EBs6GnKesyQrRMgtjOghTq5z9lwkDXmbCUythOw==\"}"},{"type":"text","text":"## Protocols\n\n- `nn-capture-discipline` applies before reading repository files; I will use the allow-listed `nn read`, `nn grep`, `nn ast`, and `nn trace` operations where possible.\n- `lsp-trace-feature-inventory` applies because the review must distinguish mechanical evidence from accepted semantic identity.\n- `plan code changes from LSP Trace evidence first` applies only insofar as this is an architecture review against source; I will inspect structural source evidence before judging the package.\n- `tiered Go verification` applies to selecting bounded read-only verification.\n- `prefer DuckDB for relational JSON exploration` applies only if the package contains multi-file/nested JSON requiring relational reconciliation.\n- Delegation, Bar-build, browser, NAIS mutation, and transcript-adoption protocols are not applicable because this is an independent, read-only, non-delegated review.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_07dc770452ad3266016ace475d434481a292020b7ab04c9d44\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_7b6f7b9e62164fa8bcafc28d09c9b6bb|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace475f7d3481a2bd31ddc7eb40f4b0","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"nn skills list","timeout":120}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":24742,"output":259,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":46,"totalTokens":25001,"cost":{"input":0.098968,"output":0.005180000000000001,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.104148}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791903577978,"responseId":"resp_07dc770452ad3266016ace475b329081a2a00bc0f95ba60b78","rawStopReason":"completed","thinkingLevel":"minimal"},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T14:59:43.780Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_7b6f7b9e62164fa8bcafc28d09c9b6bb|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace475f7d3481a2bd31ddc7eb40f4b0","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"  nn-capture-discipline        Use when about to take any action that introduces new information not already in the conversation. Load with `nn skills get nn-capture-discipline`.\n  nn-guide                     \"Use when you need an nn command, flag, syntax, semantics, usage pattern, or command-reference lookup; for iterative or human-driven graph navigation, use nn-navigate instead. Load with `nn skills get nn-guide`.\"\n  nn-link-suggester            Use when after nn new or nn update to discover notes that should be linked to the modified note. Load with `nn skills get nn-link-suggester`.\n  nn-navigate                  \"Use when a human iteratively navigates the nn graph or asks to teleport, orient, recenter, peek, scan, Integrate a bounded notebook edit, invoke positioned Navigation Ask, arrive, use history, or manage bookmarks. Standalone `nn ask` is owned by `nn-guide`. Load the compact core, then each applicable owner.\"\n  nn-refine                    Use when cleaning up a specific note or before promoting it — runs atomicity, link, and title checks. Load with `nn skills get nn-refine`.\n  nn-refine-workflow           Use when running a hygiene pass across multiple notes at once — drafts, orphans, long notes, or a topic cluster. Load with `nn skills get nn-refine-workflow`.\n  nn-session-debrief           Use when ending a session to consolidate captures, assess promotion eligibility, and update the daily page. For weekly review use --weekly; for daily page only use --daily; for lightweight mid-session capture use --partial. Load with `nn skills get nn-session-debrief`.\n  nn-transcript                Observe recorded agent work, investigate questions across transcripts, and preserve useful learnings in nn. Supports Claude Code, Codex, sdk-cli, and Pi. Use for recent work, failures, assignments, handoffs, usage, recurring patterns, or learning capture.\n  nn-workflow                  Use when asked to organise, capture, or link notes in the Zettelkasten. Load with `nn skills get nn-workflow`.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791903583779},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T14:59:43.780Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"system","content":"","timestamp":1791903583781,"toolsAdded":[{"name":"ask_user_question","description":"Ask the user one or more structured questions during execution. Use when you need to:\n1. Gather user preferences or requirements\n2. Clarify ambiguous instructions\n3. Get decisions on implementation choices as you work\n4. Offer choices to the user about what direction to take\n\nPreview feature:\nUse the optional `preview` field on an option when presenting a concrete artifact the user needs to compare visually: an ASCII mockup, a code snippet, a diagram or configuration variation. It renders as markdown in a pane below the options while that option is highlighted. Do not use it for simple preference questions where the label and description already say enough.\n\nMulti-select:\nSet `multiSelect: true` on a question when several answers can hold at once — \"which of these packages should change\", \"which checks to run before merging\". Keep mutually exclusive choices single-select; that is still the default and the common case. A multi-select question may have 2-6 options instead of 2-4, renders as checkboxes, and the user toggles rows with Space or a digit and confirms with Enter. The answer comes back as the chosen labels joined with \", \", and the user may add a typed value to the checked ones through the \"Type something.\" row. `preview` works on multi-select options too.\n\nUsage notes:\n- The user can pick an option with the number keys, type a custom answer via the automatically appended \"Type something.\" row, attach a note to their choice by pressing n, or press Esc to decline. Do NOT author \"Other\" or \"Type something.\" labels yourself — reserved labels are rejected at runtime.\n- If you recommend a specific option, make it the first option and add \"(Recommended)\" at the end of the label.\n- Ask 1-4 questions per call, each with 2-4 options (2-6 when `multiSelect` is true). Multiple questions render as tabs the user cycles with Tab; every question must be answered before the call returns. Group questions that belong to one decision rather than asking them in separate calls, but do not pad a single decision into several questions.\n\nCodemode: `tools.ask_user_question(args)` resolves to a string.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["questions"],"properties":{"questions":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["question","header","options"],"properties":{"question":{"type":"string","description":"The complete question to ask the user. Should be clear, specific, and end with a question mark."},"header":{"type":"string","description":"MAX 16 CHARACTERS — hard limit, requests over the limit are rejected. Very short chip/tag shown next to the question. Examples: \"Auth method\", \"Library\", \"Approach\"."},"multiSelect":{"type":"boolean","description":"Render this question as checkboxes so the user can pick more than one option. Use it when several answers can hold at once (\"which of these should change\", \"which checks to run before merging\"); keep mutually exclusive choices single-select. Multi-select questions may have 2-6 options instead of 2-4. The user toggles rows with Space or a digit and confirms with Enter, and the answer comes back as the chosen labels joined with \", \"."},"options":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["label","description"],"properties":{"label":{"type":"string","description":"The display text for this option that the user will see and select. Aim for 1-5 words, but there is no hard limit: a longer label is fine when it genuinely helps, and long labels wrap in the dialog rather than being rejected."},"description":{"type":"string","description":"Explanation of what this option means or what will happen if chosen. Useful for providing context about trade-offs or implications."},"preview":{"type":"string","description":"Optional markdown shown in a pane below the options while this option is highlighted. Use for concrete artifacts the user needs to compare: ASCII mockups, code snippets, diagram or configuration variations. Do NOT use it for simple preference questions where the label and description already say enough."}}},"description":"The available choices for this question. Must have 2-4 options (2-6 when multiSelect is true), each a distinct choice; without multiSelect they must also be mutually exclusive. The 'Type something.' row is appended automatically — do NOT author it.","minItems":2,"maxItems":6}}},"description":"Questions to ask the user. 1-4 questions; the user cycles between them with Tab and answers each one.","minItems":1,"maxItems":4}}}},{"name":"mcp__lsp_trace__lsp_session_v1_derive_workspace","description":"Derive READY session for exact registered Git worktree from READY parent. This is a live local operation requiring input matching https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/input-session-derive-workspace.v1.schema.json and returning a MCP result envelope from https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/envelope-result.v1.schema.json, https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/envelope-domain-error.v1.schema.json. Results are evidence bounded by the named schemas and do not establish source completeness, runtime execution, producer authentication, permission, or production authority. If this direct tool is hidden by the active advertisement profile, call lsp_trace_v1_execute with its canonical request instead. Before live semantic analysis, call lsp_session_v1_list and use an exact-workspace READY session. If none exists and the target is an exact registered Git worktree, call lsp_session_v1_derive_workspace with exactly one READY parent and the target's canonical absolute local file: URI; continue only from its READY result. Do not start an independently configured replacement language server. Choose the transport explicitly: Direct MCP operation calls pass that operation's arguments directly; for MCP gateway `lsp_trace_v1_execute`, operation is nested beneath `request`, for example {\"request\":{\"operation\":\"lsp_trace_v2_structural_context\",\"arguments\":{...}}}; CLI `lsp-trace execute` accepts production execution requests and is not an MCP dispatcher. MCP wire and server operation names are canonical unqualified names; host adapters may display namespace-qualified names. `request.operation` always uses the canonical unqualified operation name. If capabilities or the installed revision advertise an operation but the client does not list it or its tool schema rejects it before dispatch, reconnect or refresh MCP metadata before diagnosing the language server. The MCP gateway is a dispatch interface and does not bypass stale client-side schema validation. Distinguish client or adapter schema validation from server dispatch, structural preflight, and traversal typed failures.\n\nCodemode: `tools.mcp__lsp_trace__lsp_session_v1_derive_workspace(args)` resolves to `CallToolResult`.","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"generation":{"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"session_id":{"description":"Exact session ID or unique host-configured alias","minLength":1,"type":"string"},"workspace_uri":{"format":"uri","minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["session_id","generation","workspace_uri"],"type":"object"}},{"name":"mcp__lsp_trace__lsp_session_v1_list","description":"Discover sessions and exact generations. This is a live local operation requiring input matching https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/input-reserved.v1.schema.json and returning a MCP result envelope from https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/envelope-result.v1.schema.json, https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/envelope-domain-error.v1.schema.json. Results are evidence bounded by the named schemas and do not establish source completeness, runtime execution, producer authentication, permission, or production authority. If this direct tool is hidden by the active advertisement profile, call lsp_trace_v1_execute with its canonical request instead\n\nCodemode: `tools.mcp__lsp_trace__lsp_session_v1_list(args)` resolves to `CallToolResult`.","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"detail":{"enum":["compact","full"],"type":"string"},"uri":{"format":"uri","minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":[],"type":"object"}},{"name":"mcp__lsp_trace__lsp_session_v1_restart","description":"Restart exact session generation. This is a live local operation requiring input matching https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/input-reserved.v1.schema.json and returning a MCP result envelope from https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/envelope-result.v1.schema.json, https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/envelope-domain-error.v1.schema.json. Results are evidence bounded by the named schemas and do not establish source completeness, runtime execution, producer authentication, permission, or production authority. If this direct tool is hidden by the active advertisement profile, call lsp_trace_v1_execute with its canonical request instead\n\nCodemode: `tools.mcp__lsp_trace__lsp_session_v1_restart(args)` resolves to `CallToolResult`.","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"caller_id":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"generation":{"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"session_id":{"description":"Exact session ID or unique host-configured alias","minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["session_id","caller_id"],"type":"object"}},{"name":"mcp__lsp_trace__lsp_session_v1_status","description":"Read current session generation state. This is a live local operation requiring input matching https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/input-reserved.v1.schema.json and returning a MCP result envelope from https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/envelope-result.v1.schema.json, https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/envelope-domain-error.v1.schema.json. Results are evidence bounded by the named schemas and do not establish source completeness, runtime execution, producer authentication, permission, or production authority. If this direct tool is hidden by the active advertisement profile, call lsp_trace_v1_execute with its canonical request instead\n\nCodemode: `tools.mcp__lsp_trace__lsp_session_v1_status(args)` resolves to `CallToolResult`.","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"detail":{"enum":["compact","full"],"type":"string"},"generation":{"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"session_id":{"description":"Exact session ID or unique host-configured alias","minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["session_id"],"type":"object"}},{"name":"mcp__lsp_trace__lsp_session_v1_stop","description":"Stop exact session generation. This is a live local operation requiring input matching https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/input-reserved.v1.schema.json and returning a MCP result envelope from https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/envelope-result.v1.schema.json, https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/envelope-domain-error.v1.schema.json. Results are evidence bounded by the named schemas and do not establish source completeness, runtime execution, producer authentication, permission, or production authority. If this direct tool is hidden by the active advertisement profile, call lsp_trace_v1_execute with its canonical request instead\n\nCodemode: `tools.mcp__lsp_trace__lsp_session_v1_stop(args)` resolves to `CallToolResult`.","parameters":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"caller_id":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"},"generation":{"minimum":1,"type":"integer"},"session_id":{"description":"Exact session ID or unique host-configured alias","minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"required":["session_id","caller_id"],"type":"object"}},{"name":"mcp__lsp_trace__lsp_trace_v1_capabilities","description":"Discover canonical LSP Trace tools, schemas, publication support, and limits. This is a offline operation requiring input matching https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/input-capabilities.v1.schema.json and returning a MCP result envelope from https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/envelope-domain-error.v1.schema.json, https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/envelope-result.v1.schema.json. Results are evidence bounded by the named schemas and do not establish source completeness, runtime execution, producer authentication, permission, or production authority. If this direct tool is hidden by the active advertisement profile, call lsp_trace_v1_execute with its canonical request instead\n\nCodemode: `tools.mcp__lsp_trace__lsp_trace_v1_capabilities(args)` resolves to `CallToolResult`.","parameters":{"$id":"https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/input-capabilities.v1.schema.json","$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"operation":{"minLength":1,"type":"string"}},"type":"object"}},{"name":"mcp__lsp_trace__lsp_trace_v1_execute","description":"Execute one canonical request through the closed shared transport-neutral dispatcher. This is a offline operation requiring input matching https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/input-execute.v1.schema.json and returning a MCP result envelope from https://jaresty.github.io/lsp-trace/mcp/schemas/envelope-execute-gateway.v1.schema.json. Results are evidence bounded by the named schemas and do not establish source completeness, runtime execution, producer authentication, permission, or production authority. If this direct tool is hidden by the active advertisement profile, call lsp_trace_v1_execute with its canonical request instead\n\nCodemode: `tools.mcp__lsp_trace__lsp_trace_v1_execute(args)` resolves to `CallToolResult`.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"request":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"arguments":{"type":"object"}