{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_701cd5dfb45f46dea5ef55f0f649c137|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace47629d5c81a28c91d91151acdfe3","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nid: 20260917025209-1770\ntitle: 'Protocol: plan code changes from LSP Trace evidence first'\ntype: protocol\nstatus: permanent\ntags: []\napplies_when: before delegating or performing substantive planning for code architecture, implementation seams, dependency impact, or cross-file changes when a functional managed LSP Trace session is available\nexpires: 2026-10-24T00:00:00Z\ncreated: 2026-09-17T02:52:09.846094Z\nmodified: 2026-10-10T01:07:18.466687-07:00\n---\nfreshness: aging (3 days ago — may need recheck)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n## Evidence-first planning gate\n\nWhen substantive code planning concerns architecture, implementation seams, call relationships, dependency impact, or cross-file changes and a managed LSP Trace session is functional, use `lsp-trace-investigator` before a generic `Plan` agent or implementation worker.\n\n1. **Establish the exact session:** list managed sessions and use the exact READY session for the target workspace. For a prepared worktree, derive the session inside the MCP process that will perform the investigation.\n2. **Investigate structurally first:** assign a read-only `lsp-trace-investigator`. Use incoming/slice operations for server-reported CALLS and `lsp_trace_v2_structural_context` with `PROJECTED + INCLUDE + FULL_DEFINITION` for source-bearing implementation claims. Exact positions are preferred when declarations are known.\n3. **Separate evidence classes:** the investigator must distinguish server-reported relationships, projected source bodies, locator-only evidence, typed failures, and design judgment. Textual occurrences never establish calls.\n4. **Freeze a bounded handoff:** the parent inspects attributable transcript evidence, adopts only established facts, records unknowns/failures, and writes a narrow seam/constraint handoff. Do not ask the next agent to rediscover facts already frozen.\n5. **Synthesize second:** use a `Plan` agent only when cross-cutting sequencing, contract design, or compatibility analysis still requires synthesis. Give it the frozen structural handoff and exact files; permit source inspection for details not established by LSP evidence.\n6. **Implement from the frozen plan:** implementation workers re-establish their own exact-worktree MCP gate but perform only minimal API confirmation. They must move to RED tests rather than repeat architecture exploration unless a concrete assertion falsifies the handoff.\n7. **Fail or degrade explicitly:** if the managed session, structural operation, or source projection is unavailable, preserve the typed failure. Either stop planning when structural evidence is essential or explicitly label a filesystem-only plan as degraded. Never silently substitute grep results for call relationships.\n\nThis protocol does not require delegation for a trivial single-file edit whose target and effects are already exact. It governs substantive planning, not every code change.\n\n## Links\n\n- [[20260916225113-2863|Integration receipt: Use only managed LSP Trace evidence to identify the retained source-projection V2 implementation seam.]] [grounded-by] {draft} — The evidence-first planning sequence is grounded by the retained-projection MCP-only seam investigation and its partial-adoption boundary.\n- [[20260916193017-2399|Integration receipt: Agent cb41b6b2-0b20-4be used live lsp-trace and source inspection to identify the ephemeral multi-document projection seam]] [grounded-by] {draft} — The source-bearing projection requirement and bounded handoff rule are grounded by the multi-document projection seam investigation.\n\n## Backlinks (1)\n\n- [[20260921202625-8412|Protocol: advance delegated implementation with one writer and adaptive read-only support]] [extends] {reviewed} — Extends evidence-first seam planning into one-writer implementation custody, transcript-based progress review, and adaptive read-only support.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791903588187},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T14:59:48.188Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_8e1989f6079343b792875887f9aebdde|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace4763491881a2ab74482bb2d96c50","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nid: 20260921203930-2054\ntitle: 'Protocol: use tiered Go verification instead of exhaustive inner-loop suites'\ntype: protocol\nstatus: permanent\ntags: []\napplies_when: when selecting or running verification for Go code changes, especially when package or repository-wide suites materially delay implementation feedback\ncreated: 2026-09-21T20:39:30.217621Z\nmodified: 2026-09-21T20:39:59.023207Z\n---\nfreshness: stale (21 days ago — revalidate before using as evidence of current conditions; this does not imply the historical note should expire)\n\n\n\n\n## Verification tiers\n\nChoose the smallest executable gate that can falsify the current claim, then widen verification only at acceptance boundaries.\n\n1. **RED/GREEN loop:** run named tests for the current assertion with `-count=1`. Do not repeatedly run the complete package while one behavior is under correction.\n2. **Feature acceptance:** run the affected package and direct contract/transport consumers. Allow normal Go caching unless cache freshness is itself material to the claim.\n3. **Concurrency:** use `-race` only for changed concurrency-sensitive paths, including shared stores, resume convergence, managed preparation, and analyzer/session lifecycle. Do not use repository-wide race runs as the normal gate.\n4. **Integrated acceptance:** run affected packages in parallel, plus schema pins, strict parsers, vet/static checks, formatting, and `git diff --check`. A changed shared contract may expand this set; name the dependency reason.\n5. **Repository confidence:** run the complete supported suite once after coherent integration or before release. It may run in the background and does not block inner-loop work. Exclude explicitly unsupported optional packages unless the change affects them.\n\n## Slow-package handling\n\nFor a slow package, compile once when practical, execute independent named test-family shards concurrently, and run the complete package once after all shards pass. Use `go test -json` periodically to retain package/test duration evidence and revise shards from measurements rather than intuition. A harness timeout is not a semantic failure; preserve it separately and rerun with a justified bound.\n\n## Safety boundaries\n\n- Never omit a test that directly exercises a changed invariant merely because it is slow.\n- Do not claim repository-wide confidence from affected-package gates.\n- Do not allow an exhaustive unrelated suite to block a bounded qualification when affected packages, contracts, schemas, focused races, vet, formatting, and diff checks are green and the qualification plan explicitly permits that boundary.\n- Run the exhaustive suite before final release when shared behavior or release policy requires it.\n\nDefault sequence: `named RED/GREEN tests → affected package → affected package set and focused race → coherent integration → complete supported suite`.\n\n## Links\n\n- [[20260921202625-8412|Protocol: advance delegated implementation with one writer and adaptive read-only support]] [refines] {draft} — Refines the adaptive delegated-implementation protocol's independent acceptance gate with a measured tiered Go verification cadence.\n- [[20260916135810-5919|Integration receipt: Agent 563fd038-2938-44d: audit lsp-trace test-suite latency without running the full suite.]] [grounded-by] {draft} — Grounded by the retained audit of lsp-trace test-suite latency and bounded alternatives to repeated full-suite execution.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791903588187},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T14:59:48.188Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_bdbbdc49d57245459103356c6d5b699f|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace4763491881a2a9d1cf13afcf11dd","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1\t---\n2\tname: lsp-trace-feature-inventory\n3\tdescription: Prepare and review correction-safe feature inventories from bounded lsp-trace structural evidence. Use for mechanical inventory preparation, reversible grouping hypotheses, semantic adjudication, stakeholder correction, and accepted-inventory boundaries; never use structural evidence alone to accept feature identity.\n4\t---\n5\t\n6\t# lsp-trace feature inventory\n7\t\n8\tUse this workflow when bounded technical evidence must inform a feature inventory. The inventory is external to native lsp-trace graph, inspection, filter, community, instability, and capture-set artifacts.\n9\t\n10\tLoad references progressively:\n11\t\n12\t- For evidence packet preparation, census inputs, accounting, provisional records, and reversible grouping, read [Preparation and grouping](references/preparation-and-grouping.md).\n13\t- For independent semantic review, stakeholder correction, acceptance, presentation, iteration, and stopping rules, read [Adjudication and acceptance](references/adjudication-and-acceptance.md).\n14\t- For structural command details or authority ceilings, also load the `lsp-trace` skill and its relevant reference.\n15\t\n16\t## Non-negotiable boundary\n17\t\n18\tMechanical preparation cannot accept feature identity. Technical adjacency, CALLS overlap, communities, centrality, instability, repeated labels, capture-set co-membership, or matching names are structural evidence only. They may nominate or challenge a hypothesis; they cannot decide canonical identity, purpose, value, production use, merge/split outcome, coverage, confidence, or acceptance.\n19\t\n20\tCALLS remains server-reported only. Capture sets preserve constituents without inferring cross-capture CALLS or acquiring native single-capture custody. Preserve bounded zero, `UNKNOWN`, failed/successful-empty states, and untouched ambiguity explicitly.\n21\t\n22\t## Workflow\n23\t\n24\t1. Retain a transport-neutral technical evidence packet and reconcile all seeds and counts.\n25\t2. Prepare external `PROVISIONAL` candidate records with exact typed evidence references, alternatives, rejection conditions, authority ceilings, and correction lineage.\n26\t3. Treat grouping as a reversible hypothesis. Communities and instability may organize review but do not change candidate identity or status.\n27\t4. Run independent semantic adjudication. Challenge unsupported merges/splits, borrowed union evidence, transitive-as-direct claims, and absence inferred from bounded zero or `UNKNOWN`.\n28\t5. Request stakeholder correction for product/domain meaning. Record corrections as revisions with predecessors and finite inventory-state deltas; never rewrite native evidence.\n29\t6. Accept an inventory only under an explicit external authority and acceptance contract. Otherwise stop as provisional, unresolved, externally adjudicated, accepted-boundary, or bounded-review-dry as applicable.\n30\t\n31\tThe documented CLI `census` command may be used for accountable source-symbol enumeration and batched acquisition; use only syntax printed by current executable help. Its structural output cannot accept feature identity or upgrade authority, completeness, custody, cross-capture CALLS, or Leiden admission. `context` is AVAILABLE for bounded transient live structural analysis; use only current help or capability syntax and do not treat its output as retained evidence, feature identity, architecture, safety, or authority.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20260830220254-9113 — A provisional feature inventory is an evidence-bounded stakeholder adjudication surface [possibly relevant]\n- 20260824201733-0963 — Bounded provisional feature inventory v0.1 classifies 15 cross-product challenge cases [possibly relevant]\n- 20260824205433-1035 — Coverage-bounded provisional feature inventory v0.2 accounts for 33 three-product candidates [possibly relevant]\n- 20260824191243-1140 — A versioned provisional feature identity rule classifies three products while preserving correction lineage [possibly relevant]\n- 20260825163852-0028 — The 33-candidate provisional inventory is ready for a bounded evidence-tier view [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791903588187},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T14:59:48.188Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
