{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_4658019fd98b4eeebfab860642c090eb|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace47824e8c81a28445ee599dd6eafe","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1\t# Frozen lease-source v2 architecture\n2\t\n3\tStatus: `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`.\n4\t\n5\t## 1. Ownership boundary\n6\t\n7\tThere is exactly one new logical object: a dedicated directional-raw subledger inside the existing `Manager` accounting domain and protected by existing `Manager.mu`. It records reservations, component-to-lease bindings, transfers, aliases, releases, and refusal facts. It owns no backing independently of the existing sole `callHierarchyLayer1GenericOwner`, creates no second recorder or terminal, and cannot issue capacity without a corresponding C15 lease.\n8\t\n9\tThe existing generic owner remains direction-neutral and the sole terminal/backing owner. Incoming and outgoing remain independent attempts and contracts. The subledger never merges their identities, evidence, semantics, reviews, totals, or GO.\n10\t\n11\t```mermaid\n12\tflowchart LR\n13\t  M[Manager.mu / existing accounting domain] --> S[directional-raw subledger]\n14\t  S -->|metadata + lease bindings| O[sole generic owner]\n15\t  O -->|owns retained backing| C[C15 byte leases]\n16\t  I[incoming attempt] --> S\n17\t  U[outgoing attempt] --> S\n18\t  S --> T[one terminal convergence]\n19\t  T -->|release each lease once| C\n20\t```\n21\t\n22\t## 2. Exhaustive component charge table\n23\t\n24\tEvery live retained backing is exactly one owned copy or one bounded alias. “Capacity” means the exact retained backing capacity charged by its corresponding lease, not logical JSON length unless those are identical by the allocator contract.\n25\t\n26\t| Component | Owned-copy rule | Alias rule | Required binding |\n27\t|---|---|---|---|\n28\t| prepare frame | reserve before frame acquisition/copy | zero charge only as a bounded view | owning lease for exact capacity |\n29\t| prepare result | reserve before result acquisition/copy | zero charge only as a bounded view | owning lease for exact capacity |\n30\t| selected handoff | reserve before any copied handoff | zero-charge span tied to prepare-result lease | owner lease ID + offset/length |\n31\t| directional frame | reserve before assembly/copy | zero charge only if transport accepts bounded owner view | owning lease for exact capacity |\n32\t| directional result | reserve before result acquisition/copy | zero charge only as a bounded view | owning lease for exact capacity |\n33\t| retained external/evidence | reserve before retained copy/publication | zero charge only while bounded by owning lease lifetime | owning lease for exact capacity |\n34\t\n35\tNo component may be omitted because it shares bytes, a digest, source form, direction, or operation with another component. Shared backing is represented as aliases to one owning lease, not duplicate owners or hidden copies.\n36\t\n37\t## 3. Reservation before owned copy\n38\t\n39\tBefore every operation that may create an owned copy, call reservation with the exact tuple:\n40\t\n41\t```text\n42\t(component, bytes, attempt_id, account_id)\n43\t```\n44\t\n45\tThe reservation validates active attempt/account/component, checked byte arithmetic, per-attempt and aggregate limits, and absence of an existing owning binding before allocation, read retention, assembly, publication, or other avoidable effect. Exactly-at-limit may proceed; plus one and overflow refuse before effect. Refusal records preallocation/publication/effect counters as `+1` for the reached refusal class while leaving live bytes, slots, ownership, source, destination, and leases unchanged.\n46\t\n47\tFailure precedence is exact and first-match:\n48\t\n49\t1. invalid/nil/stale/foreign attempt or account;\n50\t2. terminal/released state;\n51\t3. invalid or duplicate component binding;\n52\t4. arithmetic overflow;\n53\t5. per-attempt limit;\n54\t6. aggregate/account limit;\n55\t7. source/lease validation;\n56\t8. allocation/acquisition failure;\n57\t9. publication/effect failure;\n58\t10. terminal race.\n59\t\n60\tA later condition never replaces an earlier reached failure. Refusal is not release and does not select a semantic terminal beyond the exact frozen terminal policy.\n61\t\n62\t## 4. Lease-bearing acquisition and no escape\n63\t\n64\tEvery acquisition returns one inseparable result carrying:\n65\t\n66\t```text\n67\tAcquisitionResultV2 {\n68\t  attempt_id, account_id, component,\n69\t  bytes, capacity,\n70\t  leases[],\n71\t  ownership = OWNED | ALIAS,\n72\t  alias_of?, source_form, digest,\n73\t  valid\n74\t}\n75\t```\n76\t\n77\tFor `OWNED`, `leases` is nonempty and its exact active capacity sum equals the charged retained capacity. For `ALIAS`, no new charge is present; `alias_of` identifies an active owning lease plus a validated offset/length bounded by that lease. Aliases cannot outlive, transfer independently from, publish independently from, or be reconstructed after the owning lease is invalidated.\n78\t\n79\tNo API returns raw bytes separately from the result. No field extraction, slice retention, callback, publication, observation, evidence record, or asynchronous use may let bytes escape the result’s lease lifetime. Digest, length, source locator, remarshal, parse tree, or regeneration cannot reconstruct or substitute retained raw bytes.\n80\t\n81\t## 5. Atomic transfer\n82\t\n83\tTransfer input and output are whole acquisition results. Under `Manager.mu -> owner.mu`, success validates source, destination, component, attempt/account, all leases, capacity, aliases, and terminal state; installs destination bytes and lease bindings; then invalidates source bytes, aliases, leases, and `valid` in the same critical section.\n84\t\n85\t```text\n86\tsuccess: one valid destination owner; source bytes+lease invalid\n87\tfailure: source remains the one valid owner; destination unchanged\n88\tnever: two valid owners, zero valid owners, split byte/lease ownership, partial move\n89\t```\n90\t\n91\tAn alias may be rebound only as another bounded alias to the same live owning lease. Turning an alias into owned storage requires a new pre-reserved owned copy and lease.\n92\t\n93\t## 6. Terminal convergence and release\n94\t\n95\tNormal completion, complete-empty, malformed, protocol/transport failure, unsupported, timeout, cancellation, refusal after admission, explicit lease release, owner `requestTerminal`, STOP, RESTART, Shutdown, stale generation, callback/view/handoff race, and duplicate release all converge on one Manager terminal-release operation.\n96\t\n97\tThe winner, under `Manager.mu -> owner.mu`:\n98\t\n99\t1. freezes the immutable terminal if not already selected;\n100\t2. marks the attempt closing;\n101\t3. invalidates all aliases and acquisition handles;\n102\t4. clears every retained byte reference;\n103\t5. releases each corresponding lease exactly once;\n104\t6. checks component/account live totals reach their exact post-release values;\n105\t7. assigns one nonzero release identity;\n106\t8. removes the active attempt/slot and makes reuse available only under a fresh identity.\n107\t\n108\tLosers return false/no-op. They cannot change terminal, release identity, counters, leases, or backing. Required postcondition: no double release, orphan lease, retained byte reference, valid stale alias, or reusable old attempt identity.\n109\t\n110\t## 7. Copy/alias policy\n111\t\n112\t- Owned copy: new retained backing, mandatory prior reservation, exact active lease, one charge.\n113\t- Alias: bounded `(owner_lease_id, offset, length)` view, zero charge, no independent lifetime or publication.\n114\t- Transfer: atomic movement of the complete bytes+lease result, no new charge.\n115\t- Borrow: synchronous bounded use under the owning lease; cannot be stored or returned.\n116\t- Release: exact-once invalidation and lease discharge.\n117\t\n118\tForbidden: reconstruction; remarshal-as-original; digest-as-bytes; capacity inferred after allocation; uncharged retained copy; lease-free byte return; alias escape; hidden scratch retained beyond the operation; publication before reservation; and converting metadata/subledger reservation into a backing owner.\n119\t\n120\t## 8. Concurrency and lock order\n121\t\n122\tUniversal order is `Manager.mu -> callHierarchyLayer1GenericOwner.mu`. No code acquires `Manager.mu` while holding owner lock. No callbacks, waits, provider operations, allocations, hashing, or external publication run while both locks are held except bounded in-memory validation/install/invalidation required for atomic transfer. Terminal release uses the same order. No new mutex, goroutine, channel, recorder, or terminal is authorized.\n123\t\n124\t## 9. Invariants\n125\t\n126\t```text\n127\tI1  exactly one directional-raw subledger in Manager accounting domain\n128\tI2  exactly one generic backing/terminal owner\n129\tI3  each owned component has one prior exact reservation and corresponding active lease(s)\n130\tI4  each live backing identity has exactly one owning classification\n131\tI5  alias charge = 0 and alias lifetime <= owning lease lifetime\n132\tI6  transfer success preserves exactly one valid owner; failure preserves source only\n133\tI7  sum(component owned capacities) = attempt live bytes = active lease capacity sum\n134\tI8  no reservation/subledger row is itself C15 backing\n135\tI9  every terminal/race converges on one release identity\n136\tI10 every lease releases once; no byte/alias survives release\n137\tI11 incoming and outgoing identities/evidence remain independent\n138\tI12 authority=0, default off, CALLS_ONLY, D/R unchanged\n139\t```\n140\t\n141\tAny invariant violation is a hard stop, not a recoverable fallback.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261005230220-3632 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 private owned-method-pair lease accounting, lifecycle joining, callback drain, refusal atomicity, and compatibility [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006014845-6698 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 marked-custodial retained-notification lease accounting, callback lifetime, lifecycle joining, refusal atomicity, and compatibility. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261001214518-6991 — Integration receipt: Independent exact-byte Stage-B T4 completed-STOP lease-retirement RED-to-GREEN implementation/result review [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006023814-5955 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 marked-custodial unmatched/late retained-response lease accounting, transactional publication, lifecycle joining, and callback non-escape. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261005000642-3335 — Integration receipt: Independently adjudicate bounded ADR0011 C15 private-B4 caller result lease Increment 1 [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791903624226},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:00:24.227Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_da86498b325b47599223eb3417d95aea|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace47870a7081a290c37cca6b229f70","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1\t# Correction-safe C15 enumeration plan over current source\n2\t\n3\tStatus: `PLANNED_NOT_ENUMERATED`. No final count or disposition is claimed.\n4\t\n5\t## Scope and baseline\n6\t\n7\tSource pin is HEAD `162d796f7e33fea2c2bdb98f92e41744bb728c2d`; exact files and hashes are in `SOURCE_MANIFEST.sha256`. The historical 54-seam census is baseline evidence only. The mechanical run must first identify every prior uncharged relationship relevant to prepare frame, prepare result, selected handoff, directional frame, directional result, and retained external/evidence custody. A historical row is not automatically current or accepted.\n8\t\n9\tCandidate discovery searches current source for allocations, copies, appends, frame/result captures, byte slices retained across calls, publications, owner fields, lease creation/release, alias/view/span construction, transfer/move/invalidation, callbacks, terminal paths, and generated C15 registry entries. Source locators nominate rows; they do not adjudicate ownership.\n10\t\n11\t## Required finite outputs\n12\t\n13\tProduce exact deterministic TSVs:\n14\t\n15\t- `BASELINE_PRIOR_UNCHARGED.tsv`\n16\t- `ADDED.tsv`\n17\t- `CHANGED.tsv`\n18\t- `REMOVED.tsv`\n19\t- `UNCHANGED.tsv`\n20\t- `ALLOCATION_SITES.tsv`\n21\t- `RELEASE_SITES.tsv`\n22\t- `BORROW_ALIAS_SITES.tsv`\n23\t- `TRANSFER_SITES.tsv`\n24\t- `SOURCE_LOCATIONS.tsv`\n25\t- `UNRESOLVED.tsv`\n26\t- `COUNTS.json`\n27\t- `RUN_MANIFEST.sha256`\n28\t\n29\tExpected meaning, not expected count:\n30\t\n31\t| Delta | Meaning |\n32\t|---|---|\n33\t| `ADDED` | current/new governed relationship absent from accepted baseline |\n34\t| `CHANGED` | same stable row identity, changed source/class/lifecycle/lease semantics |\n35\t| `REMOVED` | baseline relationship absent at current source with exact deletion evidence |\n36\t| `UNCHANGED` | same identity and adjudicated semantics at exact current source |\n37\t\n38\tAll four sets are exhaustive, pairwise disjoint, and their union equals baseline plus current candidate identities under the declared reconciliation equation. No actual counts are frozen here. Any produced counts are labeled `PROVISIONAL_MECHANICAL` until independent adjudication.\n39\t\n40\t## Mechanical row schema\n41\t\n42\tEach row has exactly these fields:\n43\t\n44\t```text\n45\trow_id\n46\trevision\n47\tstatus\n48\tsource_path\n49\tsource_start_line\n50\tsource_end_line\n51\tsource_sha256\n52\tsymbol\n53\toperation_kind = ALLOCATE|COPY|RETAIN|ALIAS|BORROW|TRANSFER|RELEASE|PUBLISH\n54\tcomponent = PREPARE_FRAME|PREPARE_RESULT|SELECTED_HANDOFF|DIRECTIONAL_FRAME|DIRECTIONAL_RESULT|RETAINED_EXTERNAL_EVIDENCE\n55\tattempt_scope\n56\taccount_scope\n57\tbacking_identity_rule\n58\tsource_lease_identity_rule\n59\tdestination_lease_identity_rule\n60\tcapacity_rule\n61\treservation_site\n62\tallocation_site\n63\trelease_site\n64\tborrow_alias_site\n65\ttransfer_site\n66\tterminal_paths\n67\tbaseline_row_id\n68\tdelta = ADDED|CHANGED|REMOVED|UNCHANGED\n69\tprovisional_class = GOVERNED_OWNER|ZERO_CHARGE_ALIAS|SEPARATELY_CHARGED_COPY|ATOMIC_TRANSFER|POLICY_BLOCKED|TEST_ONLY_EXCLUSION|OPAQUE_SCRATCH_EXCLUSION|UNRESOLVED\n70\tcontrary_evidence\n71\trejection_condition\n72\tauthority_ceiling\n73\tadjudicator_id\n74\tadjudication_revision\n75\tnotes\n76\t```\n77\t\n78\t`row_id = sha256(\"adr0011.c15.lease-source.v2.row\\x00\" || source_path || \"\\x00\" || symbol || \"\\x00\" || operation_kind || \"\\x00\" || component || \"\\x00\" || backing_identity_rule)`. Paths use repository-relative slash form; symbols are fully qualified package-local names; no line number enters identity, so line movement alone does not create false add/remove. Ambiguous identities become separate `UNRESOLVED` candidates rather than guessed merges.\n79\t\n80\t## Exact source manifest rule\n81\t\n82\t`SOURCE_MANIFEST.sha256` is the input manifest and includes every six-production current source/dependency, the absent required-new production path, all four absent required-new test paths, historical C15 baseline, generic amendment, immutable v1/v2 interfaces, and frozen write-set package. Before enumeration, regenerate it from the exact HEAD and require byte equality. Any drift stops this package and requires a new version.\n83\t\n84\tGenerated outputs include their tool/script bytes, argv, environment-affecting values, stdout/stderr, exit status, and hashes. Run twice from identical pins and require byte-identical outputs.\n85\t\n86\t## Reconciliation and lifecycle checks\n87\t\n88\tFor every current candidate:\n89\t\n90\t1. identify exact allocation/copy/retention or prove alias/borrow;\n91\t2. identify reservation and exact charged capacity before effect;\n92\t3. identify owning account/attempt/component and lease source;\n93\t4. identify every borrow/alias bound and no-escape rule;\n94\t5. identify atomic transfer source/destination and failure preservation;\n95\t6. identify every normal/error/refusal/cancel/timeout/STOP/RESTART/Shutdown/race release path;\n96\t7. prove one release winner, no double release, no orphan lease, no retained bytes after release;\n97\t8. join to exactly one delta row.\n98\t\n99\tRequired equations:\n100\t\n101\t```text\n102\tbaseline identities = CHANGED + REMOVED + baseline-side UNCHANGED\n103\tcurrent identities  = ADDED + CHANGED + current-side UNCHANGED\n104\tall current candidates = allocation/copy + zero-charge alias/borrow + transfer/release operation rows\n105\towned live capacity = exact sum(active corresponding lease capacities)\n106\tUNRESOLVED count = 0 before GO\n107\t```\n108\t\n109\t## Independent adjudication\n110\t\n111\tA separate review pass, identified in each row by `adjudicator_id` and `adjudication_revision`, reviews source bytes without inheriting mechanical classifications. It challenges hidden copies, alias escape, lease mismatch, transfer partiality, release gaps, row merges/splits, transitive assumptions, baseline carry-forward, and bounded-zero/absence claims. Independence is a review relationship; no delegation is required.\n112\t\n113\tEvery non-`UNRESOLVED` row requires contrary evidence or a falsifier. Corrections create a new row revision with predecessor and finite delta; native source evidence is never rewritten. Structural adjacency, names, CALLS, or generated registry membership cannot accept identity.\n114\t\n115\tGate prerequisites:\n116\t\n117\t- both deterministic mechanical runs match;\n118\t- all manifests/checksums verify;\n119\t- every source candidate and baseline identity reconciles;\n120\t- every allocation/release/borrow/transfer site is adjudicated;\n121\t- `UNRESOLVED.tsv` exists with header only and `UNRESOLVED=0` in counts;\n122\t- no write-set expansion or architecture hard stop;\n123\t- independent reviewer returns the exact gate for this package checksum.\n124\t\n125\tUntil then disposition remains `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20260824234609-5129 — Five current-source observations renew three ScopeRationalization rows at evidence tier only [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006031020-8766 — Integration receipt: Independently adjudicate the consolidated ADR0011 C15 allocation census against current source, reviewed manifest, accepted receipts, lifecycle paths, ordinary compatibility, and incomplete structural evidence. [possibly relevant]\n- 20260814163906-4069 — The retained EASI guide does not define row-count, checksum, semantic, or rollback acceptance checks. [possibly relevant]\n- 20260909164657-8302 — Source index: September 9 Mob on On-site Agenda, Deck, and Activities [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006030408-1456 — Integration receipt: Independently review four ADR0011 C15 census ownership corrections: source-handle slice backing, persistent capture params, redundant capture result removal, and Manager source-ingress shutdown release. [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791903624226},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:00:24.227Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_e8fc379a0c1a47f9881169894895f0c0|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace47870a7081a29a33ab5dcc4486f5","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1\t# Successor impact on private interface v2\n2\t\n3\tStatus: design contract only; not a compile contract and not permission to edit immutable v2.\n4\t\n5\t## Required successor types\n6\t\n7\tA later interface v3 (or other explicitly reviewed successor) must express at least:\n8\t\n9\t```go\n10\ttype privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAccountIDV2 uint64\n11\ttype privateCallHierarchyDirectionalLeaseIDV2 uint64\n12\ttype privateCallHierarchyDirectionalTransferIDV2 uint64\n13\t\n14\ttype privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAccountV2 struct {\n15\t    ID privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAccountIDV2\n16\t    Attempt privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAttemptIDV1\n17\t    Direction privateCallHierarchyDirectionV1\n18\t    LiveBytes, ReservedBytes uint64\n19\t    State privateCallHierarchyDirectionalStateV1\n20\t    Components [6]privateCallHierarchyDirectionalComponentAccountV2\n21\t}\n22\t\n23\ttype privateCallHierarchyDirectionalLeaseV2 struct {\n24\t    ID privateCallHierarchyDirectionalLeaseIDV2\n25\t    Account privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAccountIDV2\n26\t    Attempt privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAttemptIDV1\n27\t    Component privateCallHierarchyDirectionalComponentV1\n28\t    Capacity uint64\n29\t    Active bool\n30\t    BackingID uint64\n31\t}\n32\t\n33\ttype privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAliasV2 struct {\n34\t    OwnerLease privateCallHierarchyDirectionalLeaseIDV2\n35\t    Offset, Length uint64\n36\t}\n37\t\n38\ttype privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAcquisitionV2 struct {\n39\t    Account privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAccountIDV2\n40\t    Attempt privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAttemptIDV1\n41\t    Component privateCallHierarchyDirectionalComponentV1\n42\t    Bytes []byte\n43\t    Capacity uint64\n44\t    Leases []privateCallHierarchyDirectionalLeaseV2\n45\t    Alias *privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAliasV2\n46\t    Valid bool\n47\t}\n48\t```\n49\t\n50\tNames are architecture identifiers only. A successor interface must independently prove package typing and may refine representation without weakening the invariants.\n51\t\n52\t## Required successor signatures\n53\t\n54\t```go\n55\treserveDirectionalComponentV2(account, attempt, component, bytes) (reservation, stage, reason)\n56\tacquireDirectionalOwnedV2(reservation, source) (acquisition, stage, reason, error)\n57\tdeclareDirectionalAliasV2(ownerAcquisition, component, offset, length) (acquisition, stage, reason)\n58\ttransferDirectionalAcquisitionV2(source *acquisition, destination) (transferID, destinationAcquisition, stage, reason)\n59\tborrowDirectionalV2(acquisition, fn) error\n60\tpublishDirectionalV2(acquisition, destination) (receipt, stage, reason)\n61\treleaseDirectionalTerminalV2(account, terminal) bool\n62\t```\n63\t\n64\tContract requirements:\n65\t\n66\t- reserve identifies exact component/bytes/attempt/account and precedes every owned copy/effect;\n67\t- owned acquisition creates or receives bytes only together with corresponding active leases;\n68\t- alias declaration creates no lease/charge and binds to one owning lease range;\n69\t- transfer consumes the complete source handle atomically and never accepts detached `raw []byte` plus detached lease;\n70\t- borrow cannot retain or return bytes;\n71\t- publication requires a still-valid acquisition and cannot create an uncharged retained copy;\n72\t- release is the sole convergence point.\n73\t\n74\t## Exact v2 corrections\n75\t\n76\tImmutable v2 must not be edited. Its successor must change these design-level contracts:\n77\t\n78\t| v2 contract | successor requirement |\n79\t|---|---|\n80\t| transfer accepts detached raw bytes and one `*privateB4ByteLeaseV2` | transfer accepts one lease-bearing acquisition containing all bytes and corresponding leases |\n81\t| custody metadata owns neither bytes nor lease | acquisition is the non-escapable lifetime handle for bytes plus leases (or bounded alias) |\n82\t| seven generic component slots | six exhaustive charged component classes; aliases are rows bound to owners, not charged slots |\n83\t| validation can occur after caller has raw bytes | reservation and acquisition occur before every owned copy/effect |\n84\t| one moved charge is sufficient | lease set must correspond exactly to all retained owned capacities |\n85\t\n86\tNo claim is made that these declarations compile against current source. This is sufficient design detail for a later separately reviewed interface update only.\n87\t\n88\t## Frozen compatibility and authority\n89\t\n90\tThe successor must preserve generic provider-neutral profile identity, independent incoming/outgoing contracts, sole owner/terminal, exact terminal distinctions, target-set accounting, no-history-change, disabled/`CALLS_ONLY` value equality, authority `0`, default off, `CALLS_ONLY`, and unchanged Definition/Reference behavior. It cannot import Go/gopls semantics into the generic interface.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20260922140053-0452 — Integration receipt: Map every producer-owned Program C compose predicate and the complete typed propagation chain without edits or tests. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261001214518-6991 — Integration receipt: Independent exact-byte Stage-B T4 completed-STOP lease-retirement RED-to-GREEN implementation/result review [possibly relevant]\n- 20260929163700-1955 — Integration receipt: Final generic LSP immutable identity candidate byte review and successor contract decision [possibly relevant]\n- 20261005230220-3632 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 private owned-method-pair lease accounting, lifecycle joining, callback drain, refusal atomicity, and compatibility [possibly relevant]\n- 20261005192502-3026 — Integration receipt: Independently review complete ADR0011 C15 private transaction accounting production migration to V2 account/lease family [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791903624226},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:00:24.227Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_feca552570be43c999a9ee949903b92a|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace47870a7081a2990297004ddf77b3","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1\t# ADR0011 directional raw-custody C15 lease-source v2 qualification package\n2\t\n3\tStatus: `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`  \n4\tExact requested gate: `ADR0011_DIRECTIONAL_RAW_CUSTODY_C15_LEASE_SOURCE_V2_GO`  \n5\tSource HEAD: `162d796f7e33fea2c2bdb98f92e41744bb728c2d`  \n6\tAuthority: `0`; accepted: `false`; defaults: unchanged/off; relation authority: `CALLS_ONLY`; Definition/Reference: unchanged.\n7\t\n8\tThis is a documentation-only, versioned architecture qualification package. It authorizes no implementation, production/test mutation, execution, evidence mutation, profile activation, public API/schema/configuration/registry/build-tag change, deployment, commit, or admission.\n9\t\n10\t## Decision frozen here\n11\t\n12\tOne dedicated directional-raw subledger is added conceptually inside the existing `Manager` accounting domain. It is metadata and lease coordination, not a second recorder, backing owner, terminal owner, C15 account, or source of capacity. Every owned copy is preceded by an exact reservation for component, bytes, attempt, and account. Every acquisition result carries the exact bytes and corresponding leases; bytes cannot escape that result. Aliases are zero-charge bounded views tied to an owning lease. Transfer moves bytes and lease atomically, invalidating both at source only on success. Every terminal and race converges on one exact release.\n13\t\n14\tThe package also freezes a correction-safe C15 current-source enumeration plan. Counts are not mechanically enumerated here and are therefore deliberately absent, provisional, and non-authoritative. `UNRESOLVED=0` is required before the requested gate can be returned.\n15\t\n16\t## Immutable blocked evidence\n17\t\n18\tThe following remain byte-identical blocked predecessors and are not modified, adopted as sufficient, or granted authority:\n19\t\n20\t- generic profile amendment package, `SHA256SUMS` digest `df44a8befc36ff69b7e903be2b78b5cf9fbb508538b8cf04ed5bbb7fd35b2df7`;\n21\t- private interface v1, `SHA256SUMS` digest `d36211da45adb55e83f0b112a62140d7bec5ef2076edee12c3facebbd692af7c`;\n22\t- private interface v2, `SHA256SUMS` digest `8f329e1012278a7e92220d0499047a7b486402fcc2db8d10f7b4b2dcb06feeda`.\n23\t\n24\tTheir blocker is retained: v1/v2 accept detached raw bytes plus one caller-held lease and permit custody metadata that does not itself carry all corresponding leases. They therefore do not prove lease-source closure for every owned component and cannot satisfy this gate.\n25\t\n26\t## Normative order\n27\t\n28\t1. `ARCHITECTURE.md`\n29\t2. `INTERFACE_V2_IMPACT.md`\n30\t3. `C15_ENUMERATION_PLAN.md`\n31\t4. `WRITESET.md`\n32\t5. `SOURCE_MANIFEST.sha256`\n33\t6. `REVIEW_REQUEST.md`\n34\t7. `SHA256SUMS`\n35\t\n36\tAny required write-set expansion, public/global/default change, second owner/terminal/account, uncharged owned copy, byte reconstruction, lease-free escape, non-atomic transfer, unresolved census row, or changed D/R/CALLS authority is a hard stop.\n37\t\n38\tAUTHORED_NOT_GO\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261006023814-5955 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 marked-custodial unmatched/late retained-response lease accounting, transactional publication, lifecycle joining, and callback non-escape. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261005192502-3026 — Integration receipt: Independently review complete ADR0011 C15 private transaction accounting production migration to V2 account/lease family [possibly relevant]\n- 20261005230220-3632 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 private owned-method-pair lease accounting, lifecycle joining, callback drain, refusal atomicity, and compatibility [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006021001-8737 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 marked-custodial matched ServerError lease accounting, callback lifetime, lifecycle joining, consumer non-escape, and compatibility. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006014845-6698 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 marked-custodial retained-notification lease accounting, callback lifetime, lifecycle joining, refusal atomicity, and compatibility. [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791903624226},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:00:24.227Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_c972ebe761ab45bd8cbd78f921383814|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace47870a7081a2af279dfa2b0360ae","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1\t# Independent architecture qualification review request\n2\t\n3\tReview exact package bytes at source HEAD `162d796f7e33fea2c2bdb98f92e41744bb728c2d`.\n4\t\n5\t## Requested token\n6\t\n7\tReturn exactly:\n8\t\n9\t`ADR0011_DIRECTIONAL_RAW_CUSTODY_C15_LEASE_SOURCE_V2_GO`\n10\t\n11\tonly if every condition below is satisfied for the final `SHA256SUMS`:\n12\t\n13\t- one Manager-domain directional-raw subledger; no second recorder/owner/terminal/account;\n14\t- exhaustive six-component charge table and zero-charge aliases bound to owning leases;\n15\t- reservation before every owned copy/effect with exact component/bytes/attempt/account and +1 refusal accounting;\n16\t- acquisition results inseparably carry bytes and all corresponding leases; no escape;\n17\t- transfer atomically moves bytes+leases, invalidating source only on success and preserving exactly one source owner on failure;\n18\t- every terminal/race converges on exact-once release with no double/orphan;\n19\t- explicit copy/alias/borrow/transfer policy forbids reconstruction and uncharged retained copies;\n20\t- correction-safe current-source C15 enumeration has deterministic manifests, stable rows, independent adjudication, and requires `UNRESOLVED=0` without claiming unrun final counts;\n21\t- private interface v1/v2 and generic amendment remain immutable blocked evidence;\n22\t- production/test impact remains exactly six plus four, with hard stop on expansion;\n23\t- authority remains `0`, accepted remains false, defaults remain off, relation authority remains `CALLS_ONLY`, and Definition/Reference behavior is unchanged.\n24\t\n25\t## Review outputs\n26\t\n27\tRecord:\n28\t\n29\t1. reviewer identity and review revision;\n30\t2. package `SHA256SUMS` digest;\n31\t3. source-manifest verification;\n32\t4. invariant-by-invariant result;\n33\t5. write-set boundary result;\n34\t6. blocker-evidence immutability result;\n35\t7. C15 plan correction-safety result;\n36\t8. exact token or one precise blocker.\n37\t\n38\tThis token qualifies architecture bytes only. It is not implementation GO, RED/test GO, enumeration execution GO, profile/provider GO, activation, admission, commit, or production authority. Even after token issuance, mechanical enumeration and a separately reviewed successor interface remain required before any later implementation request.\n39\t\n40\tCurrent disposition: `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261010201159-8643 — Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006235523-4470 — Integration receipt: Independent read-only DESIGN_GO review of ADR0011 C18 owner and write-set proposal [possibly relevant]\n- 20261001161357-2332 — Integration receipt: Independent exact-byte result review of frozen ADR0011 A11 disposable guard V3 execution-v1 [possibly relevant]\n- 20260725001014-8818 — The NAIS pitch committed to phased dual-running migration under NAIS go-no-go authority [possibly relevant]\n- 20261005230220-3632 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 private owned-method-pair lease accounting, lifecycle joining, callback drain, refusal atomicity, and compatibility [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791903624226},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:00:24.227Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_11acbb52bf244c1cb225f772ff9f53e1|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace47870a7081a2b4f4be1887ccec0e","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1\t# Exact immutable future write-set\n2\t\n3\tStatus: `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`. This package changes none of these production/test files.\n4\t\n5\t## Production: exactly six\n6\t\n7\t1. `sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_private.go` — required-new private mechanics; successor lease-bearing acquisition/account/alias/transfer declarations.\n8\t2. `sessionruntime/sessionruntime.go` — one Manager subledger; reserve-before-effect integration and terminal convergence under existing lock.\n9\t3. `internal/lspwire/read_frame.go` — private bounded acquisition result carrying bytes with corresponding lease source; defaults unchanged.\n10\t4. `internal/lspwire/successor_ingress.go` — conditional already-reserved bound and acquisition threading only; byte-identical if unused.\n11\t5. `sessionruntime/b4_owned_method_pair_lease.go` — sole direction-neutral owner/terminal integration, atomic acquisition transfer, alias invalidation, exact release.\n12\t6. `sessionruntime/b4_c15_ownership_registry_private.go` — generated only from accepted `UNRESOLVED=0` enumeration; never hand-edited.\n13\t\n14\t## Tests: exactly four new files\n15\t\n16\t1. `sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_private_test.go`.\n17\t2. `sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_race_private_test.go`.\n18\t3. `internal/lspwire/read_frame_bounded_incomplete_v1_private_test.go`.\n19\t4. `internal/lspwire/successor_ingress_directional_v1_private_test.go`.\n20\t\n21\tThe existing selector/package ownership remains unchanged. Future tests must additionally prove every component reservation tuple, lease-bearing no-escape acquisition, zero-charge alias lifetime, atomic bytes+lease transfer in both success/failure, every terminal/race release convergence, no double/orphan, and exact C15 delta reconciliation.\n22\t\n23\t## Hard stop\n24\t\n25\tThere is no fallback or expansion. If any architecture, interface, RED, implementation, enumeration, generation, compatibility, or release obligation requires an unlisted production/test path, historical test/fixture/corpus/golden mutation, public surface, dependency, schema/profile/registry/config/build-tag/package-boundary change, the exact disposition is:\n26\t\n27\t`BLOCKED_WRITESET_EXPANSION_REQUIRED`\n28\t\n29\tNo implementation or test mutation may proceed under this package.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261006235523-4470 — Integration receipt: Independent read-only DESIGN_GO review of ADR0011 C18 owner and write-set proposal [possibly relevant]\n- 20261004222557-4857 — Integration receipt: Independent read-only integration review of ADR0011 C15 private-B4 returned request-frame ownership via bounded caller lease [possibly relevant]\n- 20260725001014-8818 — The NAIS pitch committed to phased dual-running migration under NAIS go-no-go authority [possibly relevant]\n- 20261010201159-8643 — Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan [possibly relevant]\n- 20260930025247-0850 — Integration receipt: Sole writer attempted private B4 V5 held capability replay in new b4.go/b4_test.go [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791903624227},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:00:24.227Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
