essionruntime/sessionruntime.go:2814\tobserved, _ := m.WaitReadiness(context.Background(), readiness.ID)\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-c12-p2-v2/historical/sessionruntime/sessionruntime.go:2815\tif observed.State != ReadinessReady {\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-c12-p2-v2/historical/sessionruntime/sessionruntime.go:2816\toperation.State, operation.Failure = OperationFailed, observed.Failure\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-c12-p2-v2/historical/sessionruntime/sessionruntime.go:2969\tfunc (m *Manager) observe(id string, generation uint64, kind string, state session.State, failure session.Failure) {\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/A/CLAIM_SELECTORS.json:7\t\"manager_observed_capability_frames\": false,\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/A/capability-envelope.json:96\t\"observed_frames\": [\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/B/CLAIM_SELECTORS.json:7\t\"manager_observed_capability_frames\": false,\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/B/capability-envelope.json:96\t\"observed_frames\": [\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/DERIVATION.md:27\t2. Author **new** complete framed manager-ID1 request originals with numeric JSON-RPC ID `1`, method definition and the pinned params. The expected runtime writer (`sessionruntime.roundTrip`, `lspwire.Writer.Write`) marshals the Go `lspwire.Message` in `jsonrpc,id,method,params` field order, unlike historical ID141/142 frames which place `id` first. Prepend exact `Content-Length: <body byte length>\\r\\n\\r\\n`; calculate the length from the literal body, not an old frame. Use this new WRITE as completed frame ordinal 5 in the *synthetic B4b chronology* below. The typed manager key, the full frame, raw params, pre-call transaction and owner must all agree; do not label it a completed manager WRITE until the later test independently observes and compares the manager's actual write. Old `CORE/WRITE6` and `CORE/WRITE8` frames (ID141/142, old session and transaction) cannot serve as either case.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/DESIGN.md:15\tStart **distinct** manager instances with the declared A/B profile selectors, initialize to READY, and check actual opaque session IDs against `DECLARATION.json`, generation 1, method `textDocument/definition`, and distinct pre-call transaction and completed-owner labels. For each independently, a **generic-control-only** invocation may verify the test child and fixtures: observed manager `RequestKey{Generation:1,ID:1}`, complete actual `request.frame`, `request.params`, completed WRITE observation and selected `response.frame`/`response.result` and READ observation match the separately pinned case originals. Use fresh manager instances for subsequent private invocations so this control does not consume ID1 or contaminate the private case. No generic control is evidence of a private lease.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/DESIGN.md:19\tOn a fresh READY A manager with an actual scripted child, submit the pinned A `RoundTripRequest` and `B4DefinitionOwner` to **the existing** `m.RoundTripPrivateB4(ctx, req, owner)` once. This is the only intended semantic RED invocation. Predeclare the complete expected selection `B4DefinitionSelectionKey{SessionID: actual A session, Key: {Generation:1,ID:1}, Transaction: A declaration, CompletedOwnerKey: A declaration}`; the numeric ID alone is insufficient. The eventual positive assertion demands `result.Failure==\"\"`, that exact typed key, a completed actual framed WRITE matching A, an accepted selected READ matching A, and one nonzero **manager-issued opaque lease**. No caller-created token, captured response, digest or generic `RoundTrip` result may serve as lease evidence. Consume that lease **on the issuing manager** with the exact selection key; demand selected capture fields (manager, generation/key, transaction, completed owner, method, exact request frame/params and response frame/result and their SHA-256) match pinned A and actual observed WRITE/READ. Check A's predicted Location only after selected capture, without elevating authority, acceptance or completeness.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/DESIGN.md:21\t**Assertion order:** fixture and A4/B4a/B4b controls first; fresh-manager identity and pre-call declaration next; then private call. The *first semantic failure* is labeled `ASSERT_ADR0011_B4_PRIVATE_A_SELECTED_READ_LEASE` and, on present source, must report `ToolNotImplemented` and zero lease. Do not first demand a WRITE or READ observed from the default-closed private stub: it deliberately performs neither. A compile failure, timeout, invalid fixture, failing A4/B4a/B4b control, generic-control mismatch or test-child error is `INVALID_RED_ATTEMPT`, not the intended RED. A passing assertion due only to supplied/forged bytes or ordinary `RoundTrip` is also invalid. After future implementation, the same assertion must fail if a result exists but the lease is zero, foreign, or not bound to the selected READ; this is a future falsifier, not a current-source observation.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/SPEC.md:7\tRoot `.pi/evidence/adr0011-composed-b4-manager-id1-held-v1/`; manifest `manifest.json` SHA-256 `e2d1880bd3fc09ca6c2e1f6f186d4d387d745cc10e72522597101d1d661ceb4b`. Require **all 57** distinct `assets[]` paths to be relative, confined beneath this root, regular non-symlink files, with exactly the declared length and SHA-256; verify manifest provenance/predecessor pins independently. No regeneration or silent replacement. The manifest says `a4_b4a_b4b_runtime_validation:PENDING`, `manager_response_observed:false`, and fixture custody `accepted:false`, `authority:0`, `completeness:UNKNOWN`, `NO_PRODUCER_AUTHENTICATION`. These are predictions, never manager-issued custody. Review and pin a concrete case-input assembly before execution; absent or invalid inputs invalidate the RED.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/SPEC.md:23\t4. **Real manager fixture control:** on fresh, distinct A/B managers initialized READY, independently observe actual `RoundTrip` WRITE and selected READ against each corresponding pinned request/response frame, raw result, typed ID1, session and generation. Assert the scripted child writes the literal case response only after receiving actual definition WRITE. Labels `CONTROL_MANAGER_A_ID1_EXACT_WRITE_READ_PASS` and `CONTROL_MANAGER_B_ID1_EXACT_WRITE_READ_PASS`. These control managers are never used for the private invocation. A generic control pass is not a private lease.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/SPEC.md:31\tOne positive assertion named **`ASSERT_ADR0011_B4_PRIVATE_A_SELECTED_READ_LEASE`** requires no failure, the exact typed key, actual completed manager WRITE and accepted selected READ matching A, and **one nonzero opaque manager-issued lease** bound to that selected READ. Once such a lease exists, consume it on that manager with the predeclared selection and compare capture's complete session/key/transaction/owner/method, frames/params/result and hashes against the manager observations and pins; do not allow caller bytes to substitute. The present stub instead returns `session.ToolNotImplemented` and `B4DefinitionLease{}` (`sessionruntime/b4_definition_private.go:53–55` SHA-256 `6eae09fc60e499add86af7832d9d123eca9abd6f5ae3931cfe2cfac567df6776`). Record these exact two observations at the named assertion as the expected **semantic RED**; a failure on a missing post-call WRITE, READ or positive status before this assertion is not the intended RED. No invented `PRIVATE_B4_SELECTED` constant is required to observe the current failure.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/author_id1.py:168\t# Synthetic capability chronology: observed five predecessor frames, WRITE ordinal 5.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/author_id1.py:169\tobserved=[]; fields=[b'ADR0011-GENERIC-CAPABILITY-EXCHANGE-ARTIFACT/2',tx.encode(),b'5',b'2']\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/author_id1.py:188\tobserved.append({'direction':direction,'frame':desc(wire,f'held:{case}/cap-{i}.frame'),'frame_ordinal':i})\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/author_id1.py:201\t'observed_frames':observed,'target_write_frame_ordinal':5})\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/author_id1.py:235\t'manager_observed_capability_frames':False,'a4_runtime_validation':'PENDING_INDEPENDENT_REVIEW'}))\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/author_id1.py:271\t'expectation_precedes_response':True,'manager_response_observed':False,\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/author_id1.py:272\t'manager_capability_frames_observed':False,'a4_b4a_b4b_runtime_validation':'PENDING',\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/manifest.json:303\t\"manager_capability_frames_observed\": false,\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/testdata/adr0011-manager-id1-v1/manifest.json:304\t\"manager_response_observed\": false,\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sliceops/provenance_wire_test.go:164\tobserved, _ := m.WaitReadiness(context.Background(), ready.ID)\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sliceops/provenance_wire_test.go:165\tif observed.State != sessionruntime.ReadinessReady {\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sliceops/provenance_wire_test.go:166\tt.Fatal(observed)\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sliceops/retained_calls_wire_test.go:38\tobserved, _ := manager.WaitReadiness(context.Background(), ready.ID)\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sliceops/retained_calls_wire_test.go:39\tif observed.State != sessionruntime.ReadinessReady {\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sliceops/retained_calls_wire_test.go:40\tt.Fatal(observed)\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/structuralcontextsymbolops/executor.go:226\tobserved := len(symbols)\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/structuralcontextsymbolops/executor.go:227\td := &transientstructural.TargetDiagnostic{ExactMatches: len(matches), TotalSymbols: observed, OmittedSymbols: max(0, observed-len(matches)), Action: transientstructural.TargetActionFailAmbiguous}\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/structuralcontextsymbolops/executor.go:279\td.CandidateAccounting = &transientstructural.TargetCandidateAccounting{Observed: &observed, Accepted: len(accepted), Returned: len(returned), Excluded: excluded, Deduplicated: deduplicated, Truncated: truncated}\n\nsummary: 127 symbol(s) · 127 with references · 62151 match(es) · 6659 files scanned","truncated":true,"truncatedBy":"bytes","totalLines":62671,"totalBytes":22128114,"outputLines":206,"outputBytes":51025,"lastLinePartial":false,"firstLineExceedsLimit":false,"maxLines":2000,"maxBytes":51200},"fullOutputPath":"/var/folders/bc/qbdy42vs4jn56zwrb2y09l9m0000gn/T/pi-bash-a6f3fb0767c757ff.log"},"isError":fal