g-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-callhierarchy-layer1-generic-v3-production-admission-v2/evidence/c15/ADJUDICATION_CORRECTED.json:6557\t\"accounting_reservation_rule\": \"No privateB4ByteAccountV2 reservation/lease is called by this generic-layer site. finishAccepted explicitly emits the reservations ledger dimension as available known-zero (before=after=delta=0); under the accepted C15 semantics this is non-custodial generic observation storage, so no C15 byte reservation/release symbol applies.\",\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-callhierarchy-layer1-generic-v3-production-admission-v2/evidence/c15/ADJUDICATION_CORRECTED.json:6586\t\"accounting_reservation_rule\": \"No privateB4ByteAccountV2 reservation/lease is called by this generic-layer site. finishAccepted explicitly emits the reservations ledger dimension as available known-zero (before=after=delta=0); under the accepted C15 semantics this is non-custodial generic observation storage, so no C15 byte reservation/release symbol applies.\",\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-callhierarchy-layer1-generic-v3-production-admission-v2/evidence/c15/ADJUDICATION_CORRECTED.json:6615\t\"accounting_reservation_rule\": \"No privateB4ByteAccountV2 reservation/lease is called by this generic-layer site. finishAccepted explicitly emits the reservations ledger dimension as available known-zero (before=after=delta=0); under the accepted C15 semantics this is non-custodial generic observation storage, so no C15 byte reservation/release symbol applies.\",\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-callhierarchy-layer1-generic-v3-three-world-causal-outcome-amendment.md:216\t`captureResult` may continue to retain raw result custody, but it must not inspect or translate result bytes to choose the terminal classification. After actual transport completion and existing current terminal/error mapping, `finishAccepted` consumes `attempt.causalOutcome.terminal` verbatim when and only when `class == AcceptedTerminal`. For both W04 and W05 that typed value is exactly `manageddiagnostic.Terminal(\"successful-empty\")`.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-callhierarchy-layer1-generic-v3-three-world-causal-outcome-amendment.md:308\tThe existing `newCallHierarchyLayer1GenericAttemptLineage` candidate changes body only to copy the comparable carrier. Existing `(*Manager).RoundTrip` changes body only for the one typed pre-effect branch. Existing `(*callHierarchyLayer1GenericAttemptLineage).finishAccepted` changes body only for accepted-terminal consumption after transport. Existing `(*Manager).finishRoundTrip` remains the sole admitted finalizer and changes only as required to pass the already carried typed classification to `finishAccepted`; its signature remains unchanged.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-callhierarchy-target-corpus-v1/targets.json:122497\t\"symbol\": \"finishAccepted\",\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-incoming-outgoing-calls-qualification-v1/evidence.md:33\t→ SUCCEEDED; server-reported callers included RoundTrip and roundTripWithPrivateTransaction; outgoing calls included owner construction, finishAccepted, publish, requestTerminal, waitReleased.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-incoming-outgoing-calls-qualification-v1/evidence.md:56\t- The normal finalizer calls `finishAccepted`, constructs/publishes `callHierarchyLayer1GenericOwner`, clears attempt state, decrements workers, unlocks, then requests and joins terminal release.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/b4_owned_method_pair_lease.go:716\tfunc (a *callHierarchyLayer1GenericAttemptLineage) finishAccepted(result RoundTripResult, failure session.Failure, terminal manageddiagnostic.Terminal, after callHierarchyLayer1GenericAfterSnapshot) callHierarchyLayer1GenericObservation {\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/b4_owned_method_pair_lease.go:827\to := newCallHierarchyLayer1GenericOwner(a.finishAccepted(result, result.Failure, \"\", callHierarchyLayer1GenericAfterSnapshot{ledger: a.before.ledger}))\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/sessionruntime.go:1500\tobservation := attempt.finishAccepted(result, failure, terminal, after)\n\nreferences to \"finishCallHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusal\" — 47 match(es) (name-match only, may include false positives):\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-c15-main-convergence-successor-v1/ROW_ADJUDICATION.json:4765\t\"reason\": \"Canonical C15 classification excludes this syntactic candidate as external-library: m.finishCallHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusal is library behavior outside privateB4ByteAccountV2 custody\",\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-c15-main-convergence-successor-v1/ROW_ADJUDICATION.json:4783\t\"reason\": \"Canonical C15 classification excludes this syntactic candidate as external-library: m.finishCallHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusal is library behavior outside privateB4ByteAccountV2 custody\",\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-c15-main-convergence-successor-v1/ROW_ADJUDICATION.json:5125\t\"reason\": \"Canonical C15 classification excludes this syntactic candidate as external-library: m.finishCallHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusal is library behavior outside privateB4ByteAccountV2 custody\",\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-c15-main-convergence-successor-v1/ROW_ADJUDICATION.json:5143\t\"reason\": \"Canonical C15 classification excludes this syntactic candidate as external-library: m.finishCallHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusal is library behavior outside privateB4ByteAccountV2 custody\",\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-c15-main-convergence-successor-v1/ROW_ADJUDICATION.json:5161\t\"reason\": \"Canonical C15 classification excludes this syntactic candidate as external-library: m.finishCallHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusal is library behavior outside privateB4ByteAccountV2 custody\",\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-c15-main-convergence-successor-v1/ROW_ADJUDICATION.json:5179\t\"reason\": \"Canonical C15 classification excludes this syntactic candidate as external-library: m.finishCallHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusal is library behavior outside privateB4ByteAccountV2 custody\",\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-c15-main-convergence-successor-v1/ROW_ADJUDICATION.json:5197\t\"reason\": \"Canonical C15 classification excludes this syntactic candidate as external-library: m.finishCallHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusal is library behavior outside privateB4ByteAccountV2 custody\",\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-callhierarchy-layer1-generic-v3-disposable-c15-writeset-final-review-v4.md:42\tPinned source contains the twelve proposed pre-key refusal branches in the documented order. The integrated write-set requires each enabled branch to call exactly one lock-owning `(*Manager).finishCallHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusal` after releasing any currently held `m.mu`; nil attempts preserve public behavior without allocation or publication.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-callhierarchy-layer1-generic-v3-disposable-c15-writeset-final-review-v7.md:25\tThe corpus runner counts that harness-local return as `pre_effect_refused` and skips `callHierarchyLayer1GenericV3AssertActual` for it (current lines 2059–2073 and 2084–2091). Consequently, W23 does not causally require or verify the write-set’s proposed first-line `RoundTrip` branch, `finishCallHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusal`, immutable refusal-owner construction, Manager registry publication/refusal, outside-lock terminalization/join, or fail-closed acquisition behavior.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-callhierarchy-layer1-generic-v3-disposable-c15-writeset-final-review-v7.md:142\t3. exactly one refusal owner through `finishCallHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusal` and the existing publication/registry lifecycle;\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-callhierarchy-layer1-generic-v3-disposable-c15-writeset-final.md:404\tfunc (m *Manager) finishCallHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusal(attempt *callHierarchyLayer1GenericAttemptLineage, result RoundTripResult, kind callHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusalType, reason session.Failure) RoundTripResult\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-callhierarchy-layer1-generic-v3-disposable-c15-writeset-final.md:504\tImmediately after attempt construction and before pending-key, writer, transport, admission, reservation, worker, lease, callback, frame, result, diagnostic, terminal, or accounting effects, `RoundTrip` reads only `attempt.causalOutcome.class`. Nil/`Unavailable` and `AcceptedTerminal` continue unchanged. `PreEffectRefusal` requires the already typed method-unavailable enum/reason and zero terminal, calls `m.finishCallHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusal` through the existing refusal publication/registry chain, and returns without result parsing or admitted finalization. No public failure mapping is invented here; the independently reviewed RED/corpus must freeze it.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-callhierarchy-layer1-generic-v3-disposable-c15-writeset-final.md:506\tEvery pre-admission return finalizes the request-carried attempt directly through `m.finishCallHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusal`; it never places the pointer in the transient result field and never calls `finishRoundTrip` for carrier transfer. Every admitted return reaches `finishRoundTrip`; it reads only `result.callHierarchyLayer1GenericAttempt`, performs the existing terminal/error/result/accounting/ledger finalization and at most one owner publication, assigns the final owner field, then unconditionally clears the transient field before returning. Disabled and direct legacy nil-attempt paths preserve current public behavior and return no owner. The owner field is not the attempt carrier and remains open/acquirable after successful publication. Neither carrier field has a JSON tag, public setter, exported alias, interface indirection, wrapper, serialization, or persistence semantics.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-callhierarchy-layer1-generic-v3-disposable-c15-writeset-final.md:545\t1. `(*Manager).finishCallHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusal`, called exactly once by each §7 pre-key branch and never while its caller holds `m.mu`, records/freezes/constructs/publishes atomically under `m.mu`, unlocks, and immediately executes any returned terminal action before returning the result.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-callhierarchy-layer1-generic-v3-disposable-c15-writeset-final.md:560\tresult = m.finishCallHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusal(attempt, <current public result>, <exact enum>, <exact typed private reason>)\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-callhierarchy-layer1-generic-v3-disposable-c15-writeset-final.md:590\tAny early return after key allocation is admitted and must funnel through `finishRoundTrip`; it must not use `finishCallHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusal`.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-callhierarchy-layer1-generic-v3-disposable-c15-writeset-final.md:781\t(*Manager).finishCallHierarchyLayer1GenericRefusal\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-callhierarchy-layer1-generic-v3-disposable-c15-writeset-final.md:807\tfinishCallHierarc