RPC message yet have different frame digests. Manager tests withhold the observation for unmatched, malformed, stale, timed-out, or over-limit responses. A supervised test-owned process checks the accepted definition error response against a reconstructed frame; it does not attest to an arbitrary provider. **When optional exact-frame diagnostics are selected, replay cannot independently verify exact response-frame custody from decoded JSON plus this digest alone:** reserialization may choose different valid framing. A **frame-diagnostic candidate** must retain exact bounded frame bytes under an explicitly private owner-controlled policy, or supply a separately verifiable binding of the observed frame to its decoded response; a canonical query/result transaction need not make a raw-frame custody claim. The existing `publication.Root` can confine immutable bytes to a pinned owner-only directory and `PublishVerifiedGeneration` can check published byte consistency, but neither authenticates which runtime produced them. An arbitrary fake `Runtime` can replay a genuine `RoundTripResult`, including local observations. Acquisition-owner capture provenance, selected privacy/withholding behavior, and offline replay of the exact bound request/response therefore remain open. Do not issue a method receipt or infer `COMPLETE_EMPTY` from these manager-local observations.\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/internal/adr0011methodresult/b4_definition_composed_fail_closed_test.go:61\tmsg, _, frame, retained, e := reader.ReadWithFrameIfWithin(4096)\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/internal/adr0011methodresult/b4_definition_composed_manager_test.go:238\tmsg, _, frame, retained, err := r.ReadWithFrameIfWithin(4096)\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/internal/adr0011methodresult/b4_definition_composed_v2_gate_test.go:203\t_, _, captured, retained, err := reader.ReadWithFrameIfWithin(4096)\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/internal