{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_1fd7c1cde01a4f8585da5b5c423cc1e5|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace47a26e0c81a2b9b103baefd872c8","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"file: /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/b4_c15_ownership_registry_private.go  language: go\nimports: \n4:6  type privateB4C15ProductionSite struct {\n8:6  type privateB4C15OwnerOperationDescriptor struct {\n\n## Related notes\n- [[20260729201609-7983|Taxonomy: Current DataVista users fall into six major actor classes.]] [likely relevant]\n- [[20260729195736-5648|NAIS names six major user classes across the current DataVista systems.]] [likely relevant]\n- [[20260729232925-1832|Ontology: DataVista post-launch operation relates one platform to an unresolved operating model and its operators.]] [likely relevant]\n- [[20260818161427-2168|Phase 1 orientation selects a migration-premise boundary matrix after human quiz]] [likely relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n\nreferences to \"privateB4C15ProductionSite\" — 9 match(es) (name-match only, may include false positives):\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/adr0011_c17_c15_custody_observer_red_private_test.go:458\tmapped := make(map[string]bool, len(privateB4C15ProductionSites))\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/adr0011_c17_c15_custody_observer_red_private_test.go:459\tfor _, row := range privateB4C15ProductionSites {\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/b4_c15_ownership_registry_private.go:4\ttype privateB4C15ProductionSite struct {\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/b4_c15_ownership_registry_private.go:12\tvar privateB4C15ProductionSites = [...]privateB4C15ProductionSite{\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/b4_c15_ownership_registry_red_private_test.go:70\tif owned != 44 || len(privateB4C15ProductionSites) != 44 {\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/b4_c15_ownership_registry_red_private_test.go:71\tt.Fatalf(\"ASSERT_C15_COMPACT_44 owned=%d sites=%d\", owned, len(privateB4C15ProductionSites))\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/b4_c15_ownership_registry_red_private_test.go:82\tif len(owners) == len(privateB4C15ProductionSites) {\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/b4_c15_ownership_registry_red_private_test.go:86\tgot := privateB4C15ProductionSites[i]\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/b4_c15_ownership_registry_red_private_test.go:87\tif got != (privateB4C15ProductionSite{row.SiteID, row.Class, row.LogicalSeam, row.Path, row.Enclosing, row.OperationKind, row.Fingerprint}) {\n\nreferences to \"privateB4C15OwnerOperationDescriptor\" — 3 match(es) (name-match only, may include false positives):\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/b4_c15_ownership_registry_private.go:8\ttype privateB4C15OwnerOperationDescriptor struct {\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/b4_c15_ownership_registry_private.go:60\tvar privateB4C15OwnerOperations = [...]privateB4C15OwnerOperationDescriptor{\n  /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/sessionruntime/b4_c15_ownership_registry_red_private_test.go:78\tif got != (privateB4C15OwnerOperationDescriptor{row[0], row[1], row[2], row[3], row[4], row[5], row[6]}) {\n\nsummary: 2 symbol(s) · 2 with references · 12 match(es) · 6659 files scanned\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791903682075},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:01:22.077Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_999409e08af6427da2d12ebff3a70cd6|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace47a26e0c81a2afff465c2f55e560","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1\t# Frozen private interface contract\n2\t\n3\t## Scope and existing authority\n4\t\n5\tAll additions are package-private. `Manager.mu` is the common lock for the Manager-global one-slot directional ledger. `callHierarchyLayer1GenericOwner.mu` remains the sole owner/backing lock. The universal order is **`Manager.mu → owner.mu`**. No path may acquire `Manager.mu` while holding `owner.mu`; owner callbacks and waits run with neither Manager lock nor a nested reverse acquisition.\n6\t\n7\tGeneric Layer 1 remains direction-neutral. Directional policy is Manager metadata. No exported/public/default/global change, second owner, second terminal, second C15 charge, new mutex, goroutine, channel, callback system, or write-set expansion is admitted.\n8\t\n9\t## Exact nonduplicating custody and terminal links\n10\t\n11\t```go\n12\ttype privateCallHierarchyDirectionalTerminalLinkV1 struct {\n13\t manager *Manager\n14\t reservation *privateCallHierarchyDirectionalReservationV1\n15\t}\n16\ttype privateCallHierarchyDirectionalCustodyV1 struct {\n17\t lease callHierarchyLayer1GenericLease\n18\t slot uint8\n19\t attempt privateCallHierarchyDirectionalAttemptIDV1\n20\t}\n21\t```\n22\t\n23\tThe existing generic owner adds direction-neutral `directionalRawV1 [7]privateCallHierarchyDirectionalOwnerBackingV1` and `directionalLinkV1`. A directional `callHierarchyLayer1GenericLease` carries `directionalV1 *privateCallHierarchyDirectionalTerminalLinkV1`. Each backing owns the only bytes and the one moved existing `privateB4ByteLeaseV2`; reservation/component/ledger records contain references and metadata only.\n24\t\n25\t## Exact constants/types\n26\t\n27\tCanonical complete fields and enums are in `sessionruntime_private.go.txt` and `lspwire_private.go.txt`. Typed limits remain 32 MiB per attempt, 32 MiB aggregate, one active slot, seven component slots. Refusal stage and reason remain an immutable pair with the previously frozen precedence.\n28\t\n29\t## Exact signatures\n30\t\n31\t```go\n32\tfunc newPrivateCallHierarchyDirectionalLedgerV1() privateCallHierarchyDirectionalLedgerV1\n33\tfunc (m *Manager) reserveCallHierarchyDirectionalV1(lease callHierarchyLayer1GenericLease, direction privateCallHierarchyDirectionV1, requested uint64) (*privateCallHierarchyDirectionalReservationV1, privateCallHierarchyDirectionalRefusalStageV1, privateCallHierarchyDirectionalRefusalV1)\n34\tfunc (m *Manager) transferCallHierarchyDirectionalComponentV1(lease callHierarchyLayer1GenericLease, r *privateCallHierarchyDirectionalReservationV1, component privateCallHierarchyDirectionalComponentV1, backingID, capacity uint64, raw []byte, charge *privateB4ByteLeaseV2, source privateCallHierarchySourceFormV1, ownership privateCallHierarchyDirectionalOwnershipV1) (privateCallHierarchyDirectionalCustodyV1, privateCallHierarchyDirectionalRefusalStageV1, privateCallHierarchyDirectionalRefusalV1)\n35\tfunc (m *Manager) advanceCallHierarchyDirectionalV1(lease callHierarchyLayer1GenericLease, r *privateCallHierarchyDirectionalReservationV1, from, to privateCallHierarchyDirectionalStateV1) (privateCallHierarchyDirectionalRefusalStageV1, privateCallHierarchyDirectionalRefusalV1)\n36\tfunc (m *Manager) viewCallHierarchyDirectionalV1(lease callHierarchyLayer1GenericLease, r *privateCallHierarchyDirectionalReservationV1) (privateCallHierarchyDirectionalViewV1, bool)\n37\tfunc (m *Manager) observeCallHierarchyDirectionalV1(lease callHierarchyLayer1GenericLease, r *privateCallHierarchyDirectionalReservationV1, terminal privateCallHierarchyDirectionalTerminalV1) (privateCallHierarchyDirectionalRefusalStageV1, privateCallHierarchyDirectionalRefusalV1)\n38\tfunc (m *Manager) refuseCallHierarchyDirectionalV1(lease callHierarchyLayer1GenericLease, r *privateCallHierarchyDirectionalReservationV1, stage privateCallHierarchyDirectionalRefusalStageV1, reason privateCallHierarchyDirectionalRefusalV1, terminal privateCallHierarchyDirectionalTerminalV1) bool\n39\tfunc (m *Manager) releaseCallHierarchyDirectionalV1(lease callHierarchyLayer1GenericLease, r *privateCallHierarchyDirectionalReservationV1) bool\n40\tfunc (m *Manager) releaseCallHierarchyDirectionalTerminalV1(owner *callHierarchyLayer1GenericOwner, r *privateCallHierarchyDirectionalReservationV1) bool\n41\tfunc (m *Manager) handoffCallHierarchySelectedRawV1(lease callHierarchyLayer1GenericLease, r *privateCallHierarchyDirectionalReservationV1, custody privateCallHierarchyDirectionalCustodyV1, selected privateCallHierarchyRawSelectionV1) (privateCallHierarchyDirectionalTransferV1, privateCallHierarchyDirectionalRefusalStageV1, privateCallHierarchyDirectionalRefusalV1, error)\n42\tfunc scanCallHierarchyRawArrayV1(raw []byte, maxMembers uint64) (privateCallHierarchyRawArrayV1, error)\n43\tfunc selectCallHierarchyPreparedOrdinalV1(array privateCallHierarchyRawArrayV1, ordinal uint64) (privateCallHierarchyRawSelectionV1, error)\n44\tfunc assembleIncomingCallHierarchyParamsV1(selected privateCallHierarchyRawSelectionV1) ([]byte, error)\n45\tfunc assembleOutgoingCallHierarchyParamsV1(selected privateCallHierarchyRawSelectionV1) ([]byte, error)\n46\tfunc (r *Reader) readWithBoundedIncompleteFrameV1(ctx context.Context, reserved []byte, limit uint64) (boundedIncompleteFrameV1, error)\n47\t```\n48\t\n49\tExisting exact terminal call sites are amended only in `b4_owned_method_pair_lease.go`:\n50\t\n51\t```go\n52\tfunc (l callHierarchyLayer1GenericLease) Release() bool\n53\tfunc (o *callHierarchyLayer1GenericOwner) requestTerminal()\n54\t```\n55\t\n56\tFor a non-directional nil link, their current owner-only behavior is byte/value identical. For a directional link, each calls `releaseCallHierarchyDirectionalTerminalV1` **before acquiring `owner.mu`**. STOP, RESTART, Shutdown, cancellation, explicit generic lease release, and every teardown path therefore converge on the same Manager method.\n57\t\n58\t## Transfer primitive\n59\t\n60\t`transfer...` accepts `*privateB4ByteLeaseV2`. Under `Manager.mu → owner.mu`, success validates source handle, copies/installs bytes, moves the exact lease value into the owner slot, and assigns `*charge = privateB4ByteLeaseV2{}` in the same critical section. No releasable duplicate exists after success. Any validation/allocation/state/limit failure leaves bytes, source handle, owner slots, ledger, and counters unchanged. Nil or inactive/foreign source refuses.\n61\t\n62\t## View and handoff races\n63\t\n64\t`view...` and Manager handoff both acquire `Manager.mu → owner.mu`, validate active ledger pointer, attempt identity, owner/lease/link, slot validity, and terminal/release state, then return copied metadata and bounded custody reference. If release has won or begins first, they return false or `Release + TerminalRace` and no bytes. If view/handoff holds both locks first, it completes a copy/reference validation, unlocks, and later release clears backing; the returned custody reference cannot reacquire bytes after invalidation. Handoff is never a free function.\n65\t\n66\t## Terminal integration and exact-once release\n67\t\n68\t`releaseCallHierarchyDirectionalTerminalV1` acquires `Manager.mu`, then `owner.mu`. It validates the exact active reservation/link, chooses terminal/release only once, invalidates all custody references, clears owner bytes, releases each moved C15 lease once, assigns monotonically increasing nonzero `ReleaseID`, decrements live bytes/slot, removes `ledger.active`, marks released then reusable, clears both directional links, unlocks owner then Manager, and returns whether it won.\n69\t\n70\tExplicit lease Release, requestTerminal, detached STOP/RESTART owners, Shutdown owners, cancellation, and concurrent duplicates all invoke this method. One wins; losers return false/no-op and never release a charge twice or change release identity. Existing generic `releaseLocked` then clears generic observation under owner-only synchronization after directional cleanup; non-directional paths are unchanged. No path invokes Manager while owner is held.\n71\t\n72\t## Zero/error/refusal\n73\t\n74\tZero ledger is inert; zero state is unreserved; all other zero enums are invalid except `RefusalNone` paired with invalid stage before refusal. Nil Manager/owner/reservation/link/charge, foreign/stale identity, invalid stage/reason, overflow, limit, state, mutation, or terminal race fail without mutation. Closed-domain failures return stage+reason; scanner/selection/assembly/handoff syntax failures include `error`; Reader preserves typed result plus underlying error.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261005155312-3022 — Integration receipt: Correct and independently review ADR0011 C15 Manager ingress-owner representation, self-cost, and 1024-slot proof [possibly relevant]\n- 20261005140147-9663 — Integration receipt: Independently adjudicate Manager-wide pre-reservation ADR0011 C15 source descriptor/state owner design [possibly relevant]\n- 20260923170411-6727 — Integration receipt: Sole writer d9898f33-b423-401: managed references owner pair joined to immutable private document-symbol query target and replayable typed candidate ledger [possibly relevant]\n- 20261003154219-0058 — Integration receipt: Replace caller-blessed Unit 2 target bytes with leases derived exclusively from existing Manager-held PrepareDocument/openDocument.supply capture, preserving atomic restricted commit and bounded custody semantics. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261005194011-8726 — Integration receipt: Review bounded C15 Manager diagnostic ownership and terminal transfer design [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791903682075},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:01:22.077Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_0c7cb46e68034efeaca246d654ca4d76|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace47a26e0c81a2a9ac05f1305f1b85","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1\t# Frozen private interface contract\n2\t\n3\t**Token:** `ADR0011_DIRECTIONAL_RAW_CUSTODY_32MIB_PRIVATE_INTERFACE_GO_V2`  \n4\t**Disposition:** `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`\n5\t\n6\t## Boundary\n7\t\n8\tThis package freezes compile-ready private declarations only. It implements nothing, runs no production test, changes no production/test file, creates no public API/schema/profile/registry/configuration, and grants no qualification, activation, admission, completeness, or GO.\n9\t\n10\tThe generic contracts are independently identified:\n11\t\n12\t- `CALLS_LSP_INCOMING_EXACT_V1` / `lsp-trace.adr0011.calls.lsp.incoming.exact.v1`;\n13\t- `CALLS_LSP_OUTGOING_EXACT_V1` / `lsp-trace.adr0011.calls.lsp.outgoing.exact.v1`.\n14\t\n15\tEach constructor computes `SHA256(prefix || uint32be(len(domain)) || domain || uint32be(len(id)) || id)`, where prefix is the exact byte string `lsp-trace.adr0011.calls.profile-identity.digest.v1\\x00`. Lengths are unsigned four-byte big-endian values. This canonical binary preimage is injective across the two exact domain/ID pairs and the constructors always populate `Digest`.\n16\t\n17\tIncoming and outgoing never inherit identity, evidence, terminal state, target accounting, acceptance, or GO. Provider bindings, including `CALLS_GO_GOPLS_*`, remain outside this generic interface. The sole permitted provider field is an opaque binding identity/receipt; it has no semantic authority.\n18\t\n19\tGeneric Layer 1 remains opaque and direction-neutral. Definition and Reference data are not CALLS. `CALLS_ONLY`, disabled paths, defaults, history, and lineage remain unchanged.\n20\t\n21\t## Exact declarations\n22\t\n23\t`sessionruntime_private.go.txt` and `lspwire_private.go.txt` are normative, complete `gofmt` declarations. All introduced names are package-private. They freeze:\n24\t\n25\t- constants and constructors for both generic profile identities;\n26\t- independent direction, disposition, stage, terminal, refusal, lifetime, state, and component closed enums;\n27\t- complete profile, target, target-set accounting, frontier, occurrence, custody, reservation, ledger, view, transfer, and bounded-frame structs;\n28\t- constructors and full method/function sets used by the planned exact production/test write-set;\n29\t- exact selected prepared-item ordinal retention through Manager-owned synchronized handoff;\n30\t- opaque provider-binding receipt only.\n31\t\n32\tZero values are inert or invalid: zero ledger/state is unreserved; zero terminal is none; zero refusal is none only before refusal; all other zero enum values are invalid. Nil Manager, owner, reservation, link, charge, custody, source, or identity fails closed without mutation.\n33\t\n34\t## Custody and lifetime\n35\t\n36\tThe existing `callHierarchyLayer1GenericOwner` is the sole generic owner. Its existing C15-backed lease is moved into one owner slot; no second owner or charge exists. A successful transfer accepts `*privateB4ByteLeaseV2`, installs bytes and the exact lease, then atomically assigns `*charge = privateB4ByteLeaseV2{}` under both locks. Failure leaves source and destination unchanged.\n37\t\n38\tLifetime is explicit: borrowed input, copied metadata/bytes, aliased non-owning reference, synchronized view, and released invalidation. Custody never owns bytes or a C15 lease. A view/handoff that wins both locks may copy or validate a bounded reference; release invalidates every reference. No returned alias can reacquire released backing.\n39\t\n40\t## Reservation and 32 MiB pre-effect rule\n41\t\n42\t`Manager` owns the one-slot reservation ledger. Before any acquisition/read/allocation/provider effect, it checks the exact requested amount against both per-attempt and aggregate bounds of `32 << 20`. Exactly 32 MiB may reserve; 32 MiB + 1 refuses at `Reservation/Limit` with zero production/provider/read/allocation effects and unchanged owner, lease, ledger counters, history, and lineage. Overflow refuses before comparison. The reservation ledger is metadata only and never duplicates C15 charging.\n43\t\n44\t## Synchronization and exact-once terminal release\n45\t\n46\tEvery directional reservation, transfer, transition, view, handoff, terminal, and release operation uses the universal order:\n47\t\n48\t```text\n49\tManager.mu -> callHierarchyLayer1GenericOwner.mu\n50\t```\n51\t\n52\tNo path may acquire `Manager.mu` while holding owner lock. `callHierarchyLayer1GenericLease.Release`, owner `requestTerminal`, STOP, RESTART, Shutdown, cancellation, normal teardown, and duplicate races converge through `Manager.releaseCallHierarchyTerminalV1` before owner locking. Exactly one release wins, clears backing, releases each moved C15 lease once, removes `ledger.active`, decrements live accounting, assigns a monotonically increasing nonzero release identity, clears links, and makes the slot reusable. Losers are no-op and cannot change terminal or release identity.\n53\t\n54\t## Direction and terminal rules\n55\t\n56\tPreparation is a separate ordered transaction. The selected zero-based prepared-item ordinal is immutable and unchanged across handoff. Incoming assembles only incoming params; outgoing assembles only outgoing params. No flip or cross-direction repair is allowed.\n57\t\n58\tTerminal and disposition remain distinct. Complete, complete-empty-null, complete-empty-array, failed transport/protocol, unsupported, cancelled, timed out, refused, partial, malformed, and missing payload are not interchangeable. `Released` is not a disposition. Release is represented only by lifetime/state invalidation and the exact nonzero release identity. Refusal records exact reached stage plus exact reason. Terminal selection is immutable; release cannot overwrite it.\n59\t\n60\t## Target-set-relative accounting\n61\t\n62\tEach direction carries its own target-set identity, denominator-known bit, denominator, attempted/unattempted totals, terminal class counts, exact attempted target ordinal/outcome records, exact frontier, and ordered unattempted target ordinals. Required equations are:\n63\t\n64\t```text\n65\tdenominator = attempted + unattempted\n66\tattempted = complete_success + complete_empty + failed + unsupported + cancelled + timed_out + refused + partial\n67\t```\n68\t\n69\tThe attempted-outcome ordinals are unique; the unattempted ordinals are strictly ordered from the frontier; the two sets are disjoint and their union is the exact target set. Thus every target ordinal appears exactly once. Unknown denominator, missing role, partial wire/parse/target execution, overflow, stale/substituted custody, incomplete accounting, or bounded stop yields completeness `UNKNOWN`. A verified zero denominator means only target-set-empty; zero occurrences means only zero admitted occurrences for that exact target set/profile/evidence. No repository, workspace, runtime, language, provider-family, or production completeness is claimed.\n70\t\n71\t## Hard stops\n72\t\n73\tStop with `BLOCKED_PUBLIC_SURFACE_OR_RAW_CUSTODY_CHANGE` for any public/dependency/duplicate-owner/duplicate-charge/architecture/default/activation/write-set change. No fallback or write-set expansion exists.\n74\t\n75\tAUTHORED_NOT_GO\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261006235523-4470 — Integration receipt: Independent read-only DESIGN_GO review of ADR0011 C18 owner and write-set proposal [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006161304-3942 — Integration receipt: Trace C17 event ownership from creation through charge, append/transfer, refusal, and release [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006235514-2872 — Integration receipt: Resolve the ADR0011 C18 generic transaction owner and exact candidate write set read-only [possibly relevant]\n- 20261007001630-8807 — Integration receipt: Independent C18 split-owner and exact write-set design adjudication [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006063818-4471 — Integration receipt: Recover the exact pre-restart LSP state and reconcile all 551 structural identities without changing frozen traversal bounds or generation semantics. [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791903682075},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:01:22.077Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_06835aa6297d45f1bec109bc3098047a|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace47a26e0c81a2a32d7683451f86d0","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1\t# ADR 0011 generic directional CALLS profile amendment candidate\n2\t\n3\t**Requested review token:** `ADR0011_GENERIC_DIRECTIONAL_CALLS_PROFILE_AMENDMENT_GO`  \n4\t**Candidate state:** `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`  \n5\t**Authority ceiling:** `authority=0`, `accepted=false`, repository/runtime completeness `UNKNOWN`  \n6\t**Effect:** architecture correction only; no implementation, test mutation, schema, activation, registration, publication, admission, or GO\n7\t\n8\t## 1. Decision and supersession\n9\t\n10\tThis amendment freezes provider-neutral directional CALLS semantics separately from provider bindings. It supersedes only gopls-specific semantic assumptions in the directional CALLS qualification architecture. It does not revoke, rewrite, or weaken the accepted opaque raw-custody/32 MiB architecture or its accepted production/test write-set amendment.\n11\t\n12\tTwo generic profiles are independent contracts:\n13\t\n14\t- `CALLS_LSP_INCOMING_EXACT_V1`, canonical domain `lsp-trace.adr0011.calls.lsp.incoming.exact.v1`;\n15\t- `CALLS_LSP_OUTGOING_EXACT_V1`, canonical domain `lsp-trace.adr0011.calls.lsp.outgoing.exact.v1`.\n16\t\n17\tTwo provider bindings are independent contracts:\n18\t\n19\t- `CALLS_GO_GOPLS_INCOMING_EXACT_V1`, binding only to `CALLS_LSP_INCOMING_EXACT_V1`;\n20\t- `CALLS_GO_GOPLS_OUTGOING_EXACT_V1`, binding only to `CALLS_LSP_OUTGOING_EXACT_V1`.\n21\t\n22\tIncoming does not inherit outgoing and outgoing does not inherit incoming. A provider binding may narrow provider/runtime/toolchain/workspace/evidence eligibility, but cannot add, delete, reinterpret, relax, or replace generic direction semantics, identity fields, occurrence accounting, terminal distinctions, completeness rules, diagnostics, or review obligations. Equal bytes or shared environment artifacts permit content-addressed reference only, never semantic, evidence, review, acceptance, or GO inheritance.\n23\t\n24\t## 2. Generic incoming contract\n25\t\n26\t`CALLS_LSP_INCOMING_EXACT_V1` is provider-neutral LSP call-hierarchy acquisition with these exact semantics:\n27\t\n28\t1. A target callee is established before preparation under an independently identified target-selection contract.\n29\t2. `textDocument/prepareCallHierarchy` is a separate ordered transaction. Its complete ordered result and selected zero-based item ordinal are retained. Selection must be deterministic and target-bound; missing, null, empty, no-match, ambiguous, malformed, partial, stale, substituted, foreign, or over-limit preparation selects nothing.\n30\t3. The selected prepared item is passed byte-identically, or through an explicitly qualified exact semantic-preservation rule, to `callHierarchy/incomingCalls`. Re-encoding alone never proves original-byte identity.\n31\t4. For queried callee `B`, returned member ordinal `r` with `from=A`, and call-site ordinal `s` in `fromRanges`, the generic relation is `A -> B`. Each admitted `fromRanges[s]` is one server-reported CALLS occurrence in caller `A`; preserve member/range/request/expansion/prepared-item ordinals, duplicate multiplicity, parallel edges, self-loops, source URI, encoding, endpoint items, and exact range.\n32\t5. Missing/null member `fromRanges` is malformed. The treatment of a present empty `fromRanges` must be frozen in the exact generic profile evidence before qualification and cannot be supplied by a provider binding after the fact.\n33\t6. Complete top-level `null` and `[]` may be successful-empty only if the generic profile’s reviewed terminal policy explicitly distinguishes and admits each form. Missing result, protocol error, unsupported, malformed, partial, timeout, cancellation, resource refusal, and policy refusal remain distinct and cannot be relabeled empty.\n34\t\n35\tNo source text, references/definition occurrence, documentSymbol result, endpoint-name match, reverse outgoing edge, repository scan, runtime trace, or provider heuristic may create or repair a generic incoming occurrence.\n36\t\n37\t## 3. Generic outgoing contract\n38\t\n39\t`CALLS_LSP_OUTGOING_EXACT_V1` is provider-neutral LSP call-hierarchy acquisition with these exact semantics:\n40\t\n41\t1. A target caller is established before preparation under an independently identified target-selection contract.\n42\t2. `textDocument/prepareCallHierarchy` is a separate ordered transaction with the same deterministic target-bound selection and exact terminal distinctions as incoming, under the outgoing profile’s own identity and evidence.\n43\t3. The selected prepared item is passed byte-identically, or through an independently qualified exact semantic-preservation rule, to `callHierarchy/outgoingCalls`.\n44\t4. For queried caller `A`, returned member ordinal `r` with `to=B`, and call-site ordinal `s` in `fromRanges`, the generic relation is `A -> B`. Each admitted `fromRanges[s]` is one server-reported CALLS occurrence in queried caller `A`; preserve every ordinal, duplicate, parallel edge, self-loop, endpoint item, URI, encoding, and exact range.\n45\t5. Present empty `fromRanges` contributes zero occurrences while remaining a retained successful member. Missing/null `fromRanges` is malformed.\n46\t6. Complete top-level `null` and `[]` are distinct successful-empty source forms when admitted by the reviewed generic terminal policy; missing payload and all failure/refusal classes remain distinct.\n47\t\n48\tNo incoming direction flip, source text, references/definition occurrence, documentSymbol result, repository scan, runtime trace, or provider heuristic may create or repair a generic outgoing occurrence.\n49\t\n50\t## 4. Independent generic identity, evidence, and review\n51\t\n52\tEach generic direction has its own profile ID, canonical identity domain, schema/policy identities if ever privately introduced, target-set identity, request/response identity, occurrence ledger, terminal/accounting record, evidence manifest, reviewer scope, amendment lineage, and future qualification token. Neither direction can satisfy the other’s missing role.\n53\t\n54\tA generic profile describes LSP method semantics and qualification invariants; it does not assert that any provider implements, supports, or correctly executes them. Generic evidence may qualify only provider-neutral fixtures and contract behavior. Provider observations cannot silently become generic semantic authority.\n55\t\n56\tGeneric qualification requires independent review of exact frozen bytes, role completeness, identity-domain separation, direction correctness, multiplicity/ordinal preservation, typed failures, target-relative completeness, diagnostics separation, raw-custody compatibility, and no-effect/default compatibility. Review remains direction-specific.\n57\t\n58\t## 5. Provider-binding contracts\n59\t\n60\tA provider binding must bind, without altering generic semantics:\n61\t\n62\t- exact generic profile ID and canonical-domain digest;\n63\t- exact provider/server implementation bytes, digest, length, version report, launch argv, working directory, and behavior-relevant environment;\n64\t- exact runtime, adapter, LSP method names, negotiated capabilities and position encoding;\n65\t- exact language/toolchain/build flags/module/workspace files and immutable locators or bytes;\n66\t- exact repository revision, dirty-state proof, workspace root, target files and target-set identity;\n67\t- exact managed session/generation, limits, privacy/retention policy, request/response custody, terminal/accounting records, evidence manifest, and independent review.\n68\t\n69\t`CALLS_GO_GOPLS_INCOMING_EXACT_V1` binds Go/gopls incoming evidence only to `CALLS_LSP_INCOMING_EXACT_V1`. `CALLS_GO_GOPLS_OUTGOING_EXACT_V1` binds Go/gopls outgoing evidence only to `CALLS_LSP_OUTGOING_EXACT_V1`. No binding may inherit another binding’s provider correctness, occurrence ledger, target-set accounting, diagnostic, review, acceptance, or GO. Shared immutable artifacts require independent relevance, freshness, exact-profile binding, and role verification.\n70\t\n71\t## 6. Target-set-relative completeness only\n72\t\n73\tCompleteness is relative only to a named immutable target set and named acquisition policy. It never establishes repository, workspace, source-graph, runtime, behavioral, language, provider-family, or production completeness.\n74\t\n75\tFor each direction, freeze before execution:\n76\t\n77\t- `target_set_id`: domain-separated identity over exact target-set manifest bytes and selected policy identities;\n78\t- `denominator_count`: exact number of distinct target records in that manifest, or `UNKNOWN` when the manifest cannot be completely verified;\n79\t- target identity: canonical target ordinal plus exact URI, position or symbol-selection identity, source/revision custody, and profile/domain binding;\n80\t- accounting: `denominator = attempted + unattempted`; `attempted = complete_success + complete_empty + failed + unsupported + cancelled + timed_out + refused + partial`; every target ordinal appears exactly once;\n81\t- frontier: exact target ordinal/operation stage and reason at which bounded work stopped, plus the ordered set of unattempted targets;\n82\t- partial rule: partial wire, partial parse, partial target execution, missing role, unknown denominator, overflow, stale/substituted custody, or incomplete accounting yields `completeness=UNKNOWN` and no completeness claim;\n83\t- zero rule: a verified denominator of zero is target-set-empty, not repository-empty; successful zero occurrences over a nonzero verified denominator means only zero admitted occurrences for that exact target set under that exact direction/profile/provider/evidence.\n84\t\n85\tA complete target-set run can claim only: “all targets in target set T were accounted under profile P and evidence E.” It cannot claim all calls, callers, callees, symbols, files, packages, repositories, runtime edges, or provider behavior were covered.\n86\t\n87\t## 7. Diagnostics ownership and non-substitution\n88\t\n89\tGeneric diagnostics own only provider-neutral contract classifications: malformed generic LSP shape, missing/null/empty distinctions, ordinal/range/accounting violations, direction violations, identity-domain mismatch, target-set denominator/frontier state, limit/refusal stage, raw-custody presence/completeness class, and generic policy/schema mismatch.\n90\t\n91\tProvider-specific diagnostics own provider launch/version/capability behavior, provider error codes permitted by privacy policy, toolchain/workspace loading, adapter/runtime failures, provider-specific method deviations, environment mismatch, and provider-evidence custody failures.\n92\t\n93\tNeither diagnostic class substitutes for the other. A provider diagnostic cannot establish generic semantic validity, and a generic diagnostic cannot establish provider correctness or explain provider-specific behavior. Diagnostics are not occurrences, success receipts, evidence-role completion, completeness, acceptance, or GO. Redacted diagnostics cannot replace required opaque raw custody; opaque raw bytes do not by themselves establish semantic success.\n94\t\n95\t## 8. The 5900-target corpus is gopls qualification evidence only\n96\t\n97\tThe corpus at commit `7f09e5357b117d20449fc16097631e32d4eead7f`, package manifest SHA-256 `316afe2501aebe4195894d1334be566ae49eb32c88276ebee7b2e4d86062f44d`, and declared 5900 targets is qualified Go/gopls directional qualification corpus/evidence only.\n98\t\n99\tIt is not the semantic definition of either generic profile. It is not a universal denominator, target universe, representative sample, portability proof, conformance oracle, or completeness basis for another provider, toolchain, language, workspace, revision, target-selection policy, incoming run, or outgoing run. Another provider may reference those exact bytes only as an explicitly non-authoritative test input; it must define and review its own target-set identity, denominator, applicability, custody, evidence, and outcomes.\n100\t\n101\t## 9. Compatibility with accepted architecture\n102\t\n103\tThis amendment preserves without retyping or reinterpretation:\n104\t\n105\t- sole generic opaque terminal custody owner;\n106\t- separate Manager-owned 32 MiB directional reservation ledger, one active slot, exact release/reuse and C15 non-duplication rules;\n107\t- original-frame/result/prefix custody, byte/length/SHA-256 handoff checks, incomplete-prefix custody-only semantics, and no-history-change invariant;\n108\t- separate incoming/outgoing assemblers and wrapper state;\n109\t- `CALLS_ONLY` and disabled-path exact bytes/defaults/behavior;\n110\t- Definition/Reference qualification architecture patterns for exact identities, source/revision custody, role-complete evidence, strict terminal distinctions, independent diagnostics, target-relative accounting, independent review, and authority ceilings.\n111\t\n112\tDefinition and Reference occurrences, ledgers, schemas, identities, evidence, diagnostics, reviews, or admission are not retyped as CALLS and cannot be imported as CALLS occurrences. CALLS evidence cannot rewrite D/R occurrences.\n113\t\n114\tAny generic profile requirement that needs a public schema/API/selector/config/profile/registry/build tag, public diagnostic, public activation, global/default change, or alteration of accepted raw-custody ownership/accounting is a hard stop: `BLOCKED_PUBLIC_SURFACE_OR_RAW_CUSTODY_CHANGE`.\n115\t\n116\t## 10. Exact impact on halted private interface and frozen write-set\n117\t\n118\tThe untracked package `docs/qualification/adr0011-directional-raw-custody-32mib-private-interface-go-v1/` is halted and remains byte-identical. This amendment does not edit, adopt, activate, or approve it.\n119\t\n120\tProvider-neutral reusable elements:\n121\t\n122\t- `internal/lspwire/read_frame.go` bounded original-frame/incomplete-prefix mechanics;\n123\t- direction-neutral raw-array scanner and ordinal selector;\n124\t- sole generic owner/terminal, Manager reservation ledger, C15 mapping, exact transfer/view/release mechanics;\n125\t- transaction-scoped private bound and raw byte/length/digest checks;\n126\t- separate incoming/outgoing assembler functions as mechanical request construction seams;\n127\t- nil/disabled/`CALLS_ONLY` compatibility and history/lineage non-interference.\n128\t\n129\tNames/claims that must be generalized or explicitly scoped before any later implementation review:\n130\t\n131\t- any occurrence of “Go/gopls” as semantic authority for scanner, selector, incoming/outgoing direction, terminal, denominator, or generic diagnostics must become generic LSP profile language;\n132\t- gopls/toolchain/workspace/runtime fields must move to provider-binding records, not generic profile identity;\n133\t- the 5900-target manifest must be labeled `CALLS_GO_GOPLS_*` qualification corpus/evidence, never generic denominator;\n134\t- future qualification tokens, manifests, diagnostics, and occurrence ledgers must name either the exact generic direction or exact provider binding, never an ambiguous “directional CALLS” family authority;\n135\t- existing private names containing `callHierarchyDirectional` may remain mechanical implementation names only if review proves they do not encode gopls semantics; no rename is authorized by this amendment.\n136\t\n137\tFrozen future production/test write-set remains exactly the accepted set in `adr0011-directional-raw-custody-32mib-test-writeset-go-v1/`: six production targets and four new test targets. This amendment adds no production or test path. The exact affected documentation for a future separately reviewed amendment is limited to:\n138\t\n139\t- `docs/qualification/adr0011-calls-go-gopls-incoming-profile-plan.md` and its evidence/review companions;\n140\t- `docs/qualification/adr0011-calls-go-gopls-outgoing-profile-plan.md` and its evidence/review companions;\n141\t- `docs/qualification/adr0011-incoming-outgoing-calls-qualification-v1/` architecture/evidence/review records;\n142\t- `docs/qualification/adr0011-incoming-outgoing-raw-custody-32mib-design-v1/` only to add supersession references, never to change accepted custody semantics;\n143\t- `docs/qualification/adr0011-callhierarchy-target-corpus-v1/` only to relabel provider-binding applicability without changing corpus bytes;\n144\t- the halted private-interface package only after an explicit amendment-reviewed unhalt; until then it is not a write target.\n145\t\n146\tNo listed file is modified here. No unlisted file may be added to the future write-set without an explicit versioned amendment and independent review.\n147\t\n148\t## 11. Causal future qualification split\n149\t\n150\tFuture work, if separately authorized, must proceed in this causal order:\n151\t\n152\t1. independently review this amendment candidate and issue the exact token only for its bytes;\n153\t2. freeze and review `CALLS_LSP_INCOMING_EXACT_V1` generic contract fixtures/evidence;\n154\t3. independently freeze and review `CALLS_LSP_OUTGOING_EXACT_V1` generic contract fixtures/evidence;\n155\t4. bind and qualify `CALLS_GO_GOPLS_INCOMING_EXACT_V1` against the accepted incoming generic profile and its own target set/evidence;\n156\t5. independently bind and qualify `CALLS_GO_GOPLS_OUTGOING_EXACT_V1` against the accepted outgoing generic profile and its own target set/evidence;\n157\t6. only then request a separate implementation/test-write authorization under the unchanged raw-custody architecture and frozen write-set.\n158\t\n159\tFailure or incompleteness at one step cannot be repaired by a later step. Generic qualification does not qualify gopls; gopls qualification does not qualify generic semantics; one direction does not qualify the other.\n160\t\n161\t## 12. Rejected alternatives\n162\t\n163\tRejected:\n164\t\n165\t- one bidirectional generic profile or identity domain;\n166\t- one gopls profile defining generic LSP semantics;\n167\t- incoming/outgoing inheritance or conversion;\n168\t- treating the 5900-target corpus as a generic or cross-provider denominator;\n169\t- repository/runtime completeness claims;\n170\t- diagnostic substitution for raw evidence, semantic evidence, or provider evidence;\n171\t- D/R occurrence retyping or CALLS inference from D/R/source text;\n172\t- public schema/API/activation to express the generic split;\n173\t- changing global/default limits or accepted raw-custody ownership;\n174\t- expanding the production/test write-set implicitly;\n175\t- editing or adopting the halted private-interface package in this phase.\n176\t\n177\t## 13. Claim ceiling and disposition\n178\t\n179\tThis candidate asserts only a proposed architecture correction over the exact pinned dependency bytes. It establishes no runtime behavior, provider correctness, source completeness, qualification evidence, accepted review, activation, or production authority. `authority=0`, `accepted=false`, all runtime/repository completeness remains `UNKNOWN`, and every future evidence role remains `MISSING` or `PLANNED` until separately produced and reviewed.\n180\t\n181\t`ADR0011_GENERIC_DIRECTIONAL_CALLS_PROFILE_AMENDMENT_GO` may approve only this amendment’s exact bytes and dependency closure. It cannot authorize implementation, tests, evidence acquisition, schema publication, activation, profile qualification, production admission, or either provider-direction GO.\n182\t\n183\tAUTHORED_NOT_GO\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261010201159-8643 — Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan [possibly relevant]\n- 20260922153414-9145 — Integration receipt: fake process-target returns empty outgoing calls unlike qualified live gopls [possibly relevant]\n- 20261010202414-6801 — Integration receipt: Whole-plan integration review for directional CALLS qualification, semantic-vector adoption, and census catalog delivery [possibly relevant]\n- 20260929140005-7516 — Integration receipt: Read-only generic LSP definition and references successor correction packet after superseding gopls pin [possibly relevant]\n- 20260929162516-4180 — Integration receipt: Generic LSP proposed exact schema and three immutable policy originals for implementation contract review [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791903682075},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:01:22.077Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_b8bbeac426b44ca7a99e69476c3289c8|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace47a26e0c81a2af9290e2a3a2a18b","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1\t# ADR0011 C15 allocation census — provisional\n2\t\n3\tStatus: `ACCEPT_C15_BOUNDARY`; the ledger is accepted as a correction-safe boundary, while aggregate C15 acceptance is withheld.\n4\t\n5\t## Evidence boundary\n6\t\n7\t- Filesystem source set: reviewed manifest `adr0011-synthetic-source-pin.eb859ce7fd43d19c.manifest.json`.\n8\t- Manifest SHA-256: `eb859ce7fd43d19c674a1f22925d1cb3a29c456828571d6bb0d77a9bdfe57d4c`.\n9\t- Aggregate: `sha256:fb36a36ffb71bb4d58c5cdea3f247b5fbc749a987aca11f62683c076de7437bd` (114 files, 872462 bytes).\n10\t- Managed structural attempt: exact READY session `sk1:949e027243da188035cc5c6532c4cb10df4210f2bdde80acc58b7b7b9af5f283`, generation 1; 551 candidates, 500 selected, 51 omitted; client output truncated; authority `0`; source-graph completeness `UNKNOWN`.\n11\t- Structural evidence is locator evidence only. It does not accept ownership identity or establish completeness.\n12\t- Counts below are logical ownership seams, not dynamic allocation-event counts.\n13\t\n14\t## Classification vocabulary\n15\t\n16\t- `GOVERNED_OWNER`: accepted owner with an exact release/transfer route.\n17\t- `ACCEPTED_ALIAS`: callback/dynamic-extent view of governed backing.\n18\t- `SEPARATELY_CHARGED_COPY`: independent backing with a distinct pre-reservation.\n19\t- `POLICY_BLOCKED`: intentionally unresolved or outside the marked custodial policy.\n20\t- `TEST_ONLY_EXCLUSION`: default-off package-private instrumentation.\n21\t- `OPAQUE_SCRATCH_EXCLUSION`: inaccessible standard-library/runtime scratch that does not escape.\n22\t- `UNRESOLVED`: project-visible backing without an accepted ownership policy.\n23\t\n24\t## Reconciled seam ledger\n25\t\n26\t### Governed owners (15)\n27\t\n28\t| ID | Seam | Owner / release boundary |\n29\t|---:|---|---|\n30\t| 1 | V2 transaction table | `privateB4ByteAccountV2`; terminal request plus all lease releases (`20261005192502-3026`) |\n31\t| 4 | Manager source-ingress table | Manager owner; `Shutdown` invalidates held states, clears bytes/entries, and releases table (`20261006030408-1456`) |\n32\t| 5 | Per-source ingress state | ingress lease release or descriptor transfer (`20261005173021-0599`, `20261005175249-6916`) |\n33\t| 8 | Source descriptor transfer | dedicated V2 descriptor; released at reservation retirement |\n34\t| 9 | Request-frame capture charge | temporary request-frame lease (`20261004222557-4857`) |\n35\t| 10 | Request-frame retained charge | temporary request-frame lease (`20261004222557-4857`) |\n36\t| 11 | Caller request-frame owner | caller lease exact-once release (`20261004222557-4857`) |\n37\t| 13 | Outbound canonical header/body charge | outbound transport lease (`20261004224204-4520`) |\n38\t| 14 | Successor prefetch | reader close (`20261004231943-0245`) |\n39\t| 15 | Successor header | per-attempt deferred release (`20261004232336-5883`) |\n40\t| 16 | Successor consume scratch | per-copy deferred release (`20261004233247-1583`) |\n41\t| 17 | Successor body | per-frame deferred release (`20261004232611-2989`) |\n42\t| 22 | Provisional result-token replacement | previous manager holding released before replacement (`20261006023814-5955`) |\n43\t| 25 | Diagnostic event backing | atomic transfer to Manager history, then eviction/shutdown release (`20261005201105-5277`) |\n44\t| 27 | Fixed diagnostic history | fixed Manager slots/order; generation-qualified release (`20261005214628-6095`) |\n45\t\n46\t### Accepted aliases (7)\n47\t\n48\t| ID | Seam | Dynamic-extent boundary |\n49\t|---:|---|---|\n50\t| 29 | Notification callback view | `WithNotifications`; terminal/release drains callbacks (`20261006014845-6698`) |\n51\t| 31 | Unmatched/late response callback view | `WithResponses` (`20261006023814-5955`) |\n52\t| 33 | Matched server-error callback view | `WithServerError` (`20261006021001-8737`) |\n53\t| 36 | Owned method-pair callback view | `WithPair` (`20261005230220-3632`) |\n54\t| 43 | Borrowed lexical result | `Prepare/CommitPrivateB4DefinitionBorrowed` callback (`20261005000642-3335`) |\n55\t| 44 | Borrowed capture value | callback-scoped struct/slice views; must not escape |\n56\t| 45a | Server-request ID token | exact string/integer token aliases the governed original frame only through synchronous rejection output (`20261006040600-1604`) |\n57\t\n58\t### Separately charged copies (22)\n59\t\n60\t| ID | Seam | Charge / release boundary |\n61\t|---:|---|---|\n62\t| 2 | Private request params ingress copy | temporary params lease (`20261004230052-1374`) |\n63\t| 3 | Prepared source content | Manager source lease (`20261005175249-6916`) |\n64\t| 6 | Source-lease handle slice | exact `len * sizeof(handle)` pre-reservation and reservation retirement (`20261006030408-1456`) |\n65\t| 7 | Transaction source bytes | one exact lease per admitted source |\n66\t| 12 | Encoded request body | outbound transport owner (`20261005023155-0654`) |\n67\t| 18 | Original assembled response frame | Manager/caller response-frame owner (`20261005032901-8738`) |\n68\t| 21 | Exact result token | Manager/caller result owner (`20261005000642-3335`) |\n69\t| 23 | Accepted decoded-message clone | decoded owner released before return (`20261005043636-1438`) |\n70\t| 26 | Diagnostic metadata strings | exact metadata lease; replacement/eviction/shutdown release (`20261005214628-6095`) |\n71\t| 28 | Retained notification set | aggregate owner/lease (`20261006014845-6698`) |\n72\t| 30 | Retained unmatched/late response set | transactional aggregate owner/lease (`20261006023814-5955`) |\n73\t| 32 | Matched server-error Message/Data | error owner/lease (`20261006021001-8737`) |\n74\t| 34 | Owned pair Params | combined pair charge (`20261005230220-3632`) |\n75\t| 35 | Owned pair Result | combined pair charge (`20261005230220-3632`) |\n76\t| 37 | Persistent reservation capture params | exact pre-reservation before copy (`20261006030408-1456`) |\n77\t| 39 | Consumer capture RequestFrame | exact final-capture lease |\n78\t| 40 | Consumer capture RequestParams | exact final-capture lease |\n79\t| 41 | Consumer capture ResponseFrame | exact final-capture lease |\n80\t| 42a | Consumer capture TargetSources slice | exact final-capture reservation |\n81\t| 42b | Consumer capture source bytes | one exact capacity per source |\n82\t| 45b | Unsupported-response body | exact final-output allocation, atomically reserved and released after write/failure (`20261006040600-1604`) |\n83\t| 45c | Unsupported-response canonical header | exact logical header capacity reserved before writer allocation and released after write/failure (`20261006040600-1604`) |\n84\t\n85\tThe former reservation `capture.Result` defensive copy was removed. Result bytes now remain solely under the accepted result owner/borrow boundary; it is not a current seam.\n86\t\n87\t### Policy-blocked seams (4)\n88\t\n89\t| ID | Seam | Boundary |\n90\t|---:|---|---|\n91\t| 46 | Ordinary/public notifications | ordinary behavior intentionally unchanged |\n92\t| 47 | Ordinary/public unmatched/late responses | ordinary behavior intentionally unchanged |\n93\t| 48 | Ordinary `RoundTrip` and noncustodial P2 | outside marked custodial boundary |\n94\t| 50 | Legacy ordinary owned-pair copies | outside private lease owner |\n95\t\n96\tFormer remarshal IDs 20 and 24 no longer allocate: exact canonical `Message` size is calculated as bounded scalar metadata from decoded fields/raw spans (`20261006040600-1604`). Former policy-blocked server-request ID 45 is replaced by accepted alias/copy seams 45a–45c.\n97\t\n98\t### Test-only exclusions (5)\n99\t\n100\t| ID | Seam |\n101\t|---:|---|\n102\t| 51 | `methodCandidateTestHook` / defensive test observation |\n103\t| 52 | `ownedMethodPairTestHook` |\n104\t| 53 | outbound/after-write/params accounting probes |\n105\t| 54 | decoded/owned-pair reserve/refusal probes |\n106\t| 55 | C wire/decode/retain probes |\n107\t\n108\tAll are package-private, default-off, and excluded from production custody.\n109\t\n110\t### Opaque scratch exclusion (1)\n111\t\n112\t| ID | Seam | Boundary |\n113\t|---:|---|---|\n114\t| 19 | `encoding/json` decoder/runtime internals | inaccessible transient backing; excluded unless project-visible backing escapes |\n115\t\n116\t### Lifecycle join (cross-cutting)\n117\t\n118\t| ID | Seam | Boundary |\n119\t|---:|---|---|\n120\t| 56 | STOP/RESTART retirement join | terminal admission closure and post-Manager-unlock wait for pair, notification, server-error, and response owners |\n121\t\n122\tID 56 is cross-cutting and is included in the governed-owner count through the owners it joins; it is not an additional backing allocation.\n123\t\n124\t## Count reconciliation\n125\t\n126\t```text\n127\tlogical backing seams = 54\n128\t54 = 15 GOVERNED_OWNER\n129\t   + 7 ACCEPTED_ALIAS\n130\t   + 22 SEPARATELY_CHARGED_COPY\n131\t   + 4 POLICY_BLOCKED\n132\t   + 5 TEST_ONLY_EXCLUSION\n133\t   + 1 OPAQUE_SCRATCH_EXCLUSION\n134\t   + 0 unclassified backing in the reconciled filesystem census\n135\t```\n136\t\n137\tCross-cutting lifecycle join ID 56 and removed historical result-copy ID 38 are not counted as current backing seams.\n138\t\n139\t## Gap ledger\n140\t\n141\t| Gap | State | Revisit condition |\n142\t|---|---|---|\n143\t| Incoming server requests | `ACCEPTED_PARTIAL` | governed synchronous MethodNotFound rejection; no caller publication (`20261006040600-1604`) |\n144\t| Complete-message and diagnostic remarshal | `ACCEPTED_PARTIAL` | allocation-free exact canonical size calculation (`20261006040600-1604`) |\n145\t| Managed structural evidence | `BLOCKED_CAPABILITY_GAP` | all 551 identities are required; current API exposes only 500 identities plus aggregate omitted=51; authority remains 0 |\n146\t| Dirty worktree identity | `ACCEPTED_BOUNDARY` | exact reviewed source manifest above identifies selected implementation bytes; it is not build identity |\n147\t| Aggregate receipt | `NOT_ACCEPTED` | independent consolidated semantic review of this census and terminal accounting |\n148\t\n149\t## Falsifier\n150\t\n151\tThis census is false if any marked custodial production path allocates, copies, aliases, transfers, or retains project-visible backing not represented above; retains governed backing after its listed terminal release; lets a callback view escape; publishes a governed server request instead of synchronously rejecting it; or permits ordinary/public paths to enter private custody.\n152\t\n153\t## Evidence ceiling\n154\t\n155\tThis document is a provisional ownership ledger, not C15 completion, runtime proof, production authority, source-graph completeness, C16/C17 qualification, or public enablement.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261006030408-1456 — Integration receipt: Independently review four ADR0011 C15 census ownership corrections: source-handle slice backing, persistent capture params, redundant capture result removal, and Manager source-ingress shutdown release. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006023814-5955 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 marked-custodial unmatched/late retained-response lease accounting, transactional publication, lifecycle joining, and callback non-escape. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006040925-5954 — Integration receipt: Final consolidated adjudication of updated ADR0011 C15 allocation boundary after remarshal elimination and governed server-request handling. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261005140147-9663 — Integration receipt: Independently adjudicate Manager-wide pre-reservation ADR0011 C15 source descriptor/state owner design [possibly relevant]\n- 20261005230220-3632 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 private owned-method-pair lease accounting, lifecycle joining, callback drain, refusal atomicity, and compatibility