HCYNhVkpKSAJSq6pRBb02Jwb4--SXN1rUyhD7NaPqolxAd_BMOMA==\"}"},{"type":"text","text":"“Whole-file predecessor locks turn small retained-evidence updates into transitive hash-renewal cascades.”\n\nSelected because: score `1` and match_reason `\"body, title, outbound\"` match predecessor-lock and hash-renewal concerns, though relevance to this package remains to be established.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_07dc770452ad3266016ace48dcd14c81a28ff6942433694e60\",\"phase\":\"commentary\"}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_f0b7147280604dd091f70408d64981df|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace48ddb51481a295c53fafd9ac3997","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"nn show 20260824155530-1135","timeout":120}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":181959,"output":109,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":10,"totalTokens":182068,"cost":{"input":0.7278359999999999,"output":0.00218,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.7300159999999999}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791903961535,"responseId":"resp_07dc770452ad3266016ace48da244481a2bfe94128f0db5106","rawStopReason":"completed","thinkingLevel":"minimal"},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:06:07.726Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_f0b7147280604dd091f70408d64981df|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace48ddb51481a295c53fafd9ac3997","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nid: 20260824155530-1135\ntitle: Whole-file predecessor locks turn small retained-evidence updates into transitive hash-renewal cascades\ntype: observation\nstatus: reviewed\ntags:\n    - nais\n    - provenance\n    - sha256\n    - retained-lifecycle\n    - technical-debt\n    - drift-detection\n    - evidence-boundary\ncreated: 2026-08-24T15:55:30.769428Z\nmodified: 2026-09-11T08:01:19.320202-07:00\n---\nfreshness: stale (32 days ago — revalidate before using as evidence of current conditions; this does not imply the historical note should expire)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDuring the guarded operational-continuity risk update committed as `a88c53e`, changing one canonical Issue 58 risk row and its active projection caused downstream retained-lifecycle failures in Issues 64, 65, 66, and 69. Each package protected a whole-file SHA-256 identity directly or transitively, so the semantically bounded update required four expected-hash renewals before the full lifecycle passed.\n\nThe mechanism provides effective drift detection, but it is not immutable historical provenance when expected hashes are replaced in place. It behaves as a mutable compatibility lock: unnoticed predecessor changes fail, while reviewed successor bytes overwrite the expected identity. This is brittle because unrelated or narrowly scoped predecessor changes can transitively invalidate packages whose substantive claims remain unchanged.\n\nA future separately oriented design seam could classify locks as historical provenance, current compatibility, or accidental coupling; preserve predecessor hash history; and use scoped semantic digests or explicit versioned contracts where whole-file identity is unnecessary. No provenance-system refactor was authorized by the risk-row update.\n\nThe completed retained topology at discovery commit 2d1a9d9 established systemic mutable compatibility coupling across 34 direct locks and 20 normalized nodes while leaving each lock's semantic necessity unestablished.\n\nFor v0.6 evidence admission, canonical artifacts, frozen copies, generated projections, and receipts must be classified separately because 443 scanned files repeat all 36 stable identities.\n\n## Links\n\n- [[20260824153527-3462|Post-school-credit execution orientation selects one guarded operational-continuity risk delta]] [grounded-by] — The selected receiver delta exposed the transitive whole-file hash-renewal cost during implementation.\n- [[20260818205743-4778|Supporting census separates the first-pass NAIS risk register into validation, decision-risk, and authority-blocker classes]] [grounded-by] — The guarded risk-register package was the changed predecessor at the root of the observed cascade.\n\n## Backlinks (3)\n\n- [[20260824153527-3462|Post-school-credit execution orientation selects one guarded operational-continuity risk delta]] [source-of] {draft} — Implementation of the selected guarded risk delta exposed this four-package hash-renewal cascade.\n- [[20260824164328-3791|Engagement-wide orientation selects retained provenance-lock dependency topology]] [grounded-by] — The observed four-package renewal cascade grounds the unresolved denominator and prevalence question.\n- [[20260824165807-1481|Withdrawn orientation: semantic-use census fails marginal decision-value gate]] [grounded-by] — The observed renewal cascade and mutable compatibility mechanism ground the evidence-absorption consequence.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791903967726},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:06:07.726Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
