4|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace48e820b081a2aa47fc07feb0c9a8","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"nn read /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-directional-raw-custody-c15-lease-source-v2-go-v1/WRITESET.md","timeout":120}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_358ee9d4a1ac45e28ded0862ae3f1c2d|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace48e820b081a2951beb580a20124a","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"nn read /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-directional-raw-custody-c15-lease-source-v2-go-v1/SHA256SUMS","timeout":120}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_99d5fda443d546d688aa96d9a1e51b1d|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace48e820b081a2886106330e53b11b","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"nn read /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m/docs/qualification/adr0011-directional-raw-custody-c15-lease-source-v2-go-v1/SOURCE_MANIFEST.sha256","timeout":120}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_773da26e658d4b96927e924764722bc0|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace48e820b081a29f82dbedeb4d739a","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"git -C /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m rev-parse HEAD; git -C /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m status --porcelain=v1 --untracked-files=all; git -C /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m diff --name-only; git -C /private/tmp/adr0011-incoming-calls-v1-6yiY4m diff --cached --name-only","timeout":120}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_044f70430e134df3b5c4fecd0be909b7|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace48e820b081a29cc21f6557bad4d5","name":"mcp__lsp_trace__lsp_session_v1_status","arguments":{"session_id":"sk1:9056e071454cbbd51661782b2964d4a8d5c266675df42622d95c5d5032abf0f9","generation":1,"detail":"compact"}}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.6-sol","usage":{"input":1011,"output":770,"cacheRead":181760,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":17,"totalTokens":183541,"cost":{"input":0.004044,"output":0.0154,"cacheRead":0.072704,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.09214800000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1791903967729,"responseId":"resp_07dc770452ad3266016ace48e0384481a29802551440cbddd4","rawStopReason":"completed","thinkingLevel":"minimal"},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:06:17.291Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_f0435a4434f440b0934b52b2d58ed227|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace48e398a481a28240664addd7a06e","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1\t# Frozen lease-source v2 architecture\n2\t\n3\tStatus: `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`.\n4\t\n5\t## 1. Ownership boundary\n6\t\n7\tThere is exactly one new logical object: a dedicated directional-raw subledger inside the existing `Manager` accounting domain and protected by existing `Manager.mu`. It records reservations, component-to-lease bindings, transfers, aliases, releases, and refusal facts. It owns no backing independently of the existing sole `callHierarchyLayer1GenericOwner`, creates no second recorder or terminal, and cannot issue capacity without a corresponding C15 lease.\n8\t\n9\tThe existing generic owner remains direction-neutral and the sole terminal/backing owner. Incoming and outgoing remain independent attempts and contracts. The subledger never merges their identities, evidence, semantics, reviews, totals, or GO.\n10\t\n11\t```mermaid\n12\tflowchart LR\n13\t  M[Manager.mu / existing accounting domain] --> S[directional-raw subledger]\n14\t  S -->|metadata + lease bindings| O[sole generic owner]\n15\t  O -->|owns retained backing| C[C15 byte leases]\n16\t  I[incoming attempt] --> S\n17\t  U[outgoing attempt] --> S\n18\t  S --> T[one terminal convergence]\n19\t  T -->|release each lease once| C\n20\t```\n21\t\n22\t## 2. Exhaustive component charge table\n23\t\n24\tEvery live retained backing is exactly one owned copy or one bounded alias. “Capacity” means the exact retained backing capacity charged by its corresponding lease, not logical JSON length unless those are identical by the allocator contract.\n25\t\n26\t| Component | Owned-copy rule | Alias rule | Required binding |\n27\t|---|---|---|---|\n28\t| prepare frame | reserve before frame acquisition/copy | zero charge only as a bounded view | owning lease for exact capacity |\n29\t| prepare result | reserve before result acquisition/copy | zero charge only as a bounded view | owning lease for exact capacity |\n30\t| selected handoff | reserve before any copied handoff | zero-charge span tied to prepare-result lease | owner lease ID + offset/length |\n31\t| directional frame | reserve before assembly/copy | zero charge only if transport accepts bounded owner view | owning lease for exact capacity |\n32\t| directional result | reserve before result acquisition/copy | zero charge only as a bounded view | owning lease for exact capacity |\n33\t| retained external/evidence | reserve before retained copy/publication | zero charge only while bounded by owning lease lifetime | owning lease for exact capacity |\n34\t\n35\tNo component may be omitted because it shares bytes, a digest, source form, direction, or operation with another component. Shared backing is represented as aliases to one owning lease, not duplicate owners or hidden copies.\n36\t\n37\t## 3. Reservation before owned copy\n38\t\n39\tBefore every operation that may create an owned copy, call reservation with the exact tuple:\n40\t\n41\t```text\n42\t(component, bytes, attempt_id, account_id)\n43\t```\n44\t\n45\tThe reservation validates active attempt/account/component, checked byte arithmetic, per-attempt and aggregate limits, and absence of an existing owning binding before allocation, read retention, assembly, publication, or other avoidable effect. Exactly-at-limit may proceed; plus one and overflow refuse before effect. Refusal records preallocation/publication/effect counters as `+1` for the reached refusal class while leaving live bytes, slots, ownership, source, destination, and leases unchanged.\n46\t\n47\tFailure precedence is exact and first-match:\n48\t\n49\t1. invalid/nil/stale/foreign attempt or account;\n50\t2. terminal/released state;\n51\t3. invalid or duplicate component binding;\n52\t4. arithmetic overflow;\n53\t5. per-attempt limit;\n54\t6. aggregate/account limit;\n55\t7. source/lease validation;\n56\t8. allocation/acquisition failure;\n57\t9. publication/effect failure;\n58\t10. terminal race.\n59\t\n60\tA later condition never replaces an earlier reached failure. Refusal is not release and does not select a semantic terminal beyond the exact frozen terminal policy.\n61\t\n62\t## 4. Lease-bearing acquisition and no escape\n63\t\n64\tEvery acquisition returns one inseparable result carrying:\n65\t\n66\t```text\n67\tAcquisitionResultV2 {\n68\t  attempt_id, account_id, component,\n69\t  bytes, capacity,\n70\t  leases[],\n71\t  ownership = OWNED | ALIAS,\n72\t  alias_of?, source_form, digest,\n73\t  valid\n74\t}\n75\t```\n76\t\n77\tFor `OWNED`, `leases` is nonempty and its exact active capacity sum equals the charged retained capacity. For `ALIAS`, no new charge is present; `alias_of` identifies an active owning lease plus a validated offset/length bounded by that lease. Aliases cannot outlive, transfer independently from, publish independently from, or be reconstructed after the owning lease is invalidated.\n78\t\n79\tNo API returns raw bytes separately from the result. No field extraction, slice retention, callback, publication, observation, evidence record, or asynchronous use may let bytes escape the result’s lease lifetime. Digest, length, source locator, remarshal, parse tree, or regeneration cannot reconstruct or substitute retained raw bytes.\n80\t\n81\t## 5. Atomic transfer\n82\t\n83\tTransfer input and output are whole acquisition results. Under the complete nested order `Manager.mu -> callHierarchyLayer1GenericOwner.mu -> privateB4ByteAccountV2.mu`, success validates source, destination, component, attempt/account, all leases, capacity, aliases, and terminal state; installs destination bytes and lease bindings; then invalidates source bytes, aliases, leases, and `valid` in the same critical section. The account lock is acquired only while Manager and owner locks are already held, and is released first.\n84\t\n85\t```text\n86\tsuccess: one valid destination owner; source bytes+lease invalid\n87\tfailure: source remains the one valid owner; destination unchanged\n88\tnever: two valid owners, zero valid owners, split byte/lease ownership, partial move\n89\t```\n90\t\n91\tAn alias may be rebound only as another bounded alias to the same live owning lease. Turning an alias into owned storage requires a new pre-reserved owned copy and lease.\n92\t\n93\t## 6. Terminal convergence and release\n94\t\n95\tNormal completion, complete-empty, malformed, protocol/transport failure, unsupported, timeout, cancellation, refusal after admission, explicit lease release, owner `requestTerminal`, STOP, RESTART, Shutdown, stale generation, callback/view/handoff race, and duplicate release all converge on one Manager terminal-release operation.\n96\t\n97\tThe winner enters under `Manager.mu`, then `callHierarchyLayer1GenericOwner.mu`, and acquires `privateB4ByteAccountV2.mu` only for nested lease discharge/account mutation:\n98\t\n99\t1. freezes the immutable terminal if not already selected;\n100\t2. marks the attempt closing;\n101\t3. invalidates all aliases and acquisition handles under Manager/owner protection;\n102\t4. clears every retained byte reference;\n103\t5. under the nested account lock, releases each corresponding lease exactly once and applies account counters;\n104\t6. releases the account lock before owner and Manager locks;\n105\t7. checks component/account live totals reach their exact post-release values;\n106\t8. assigns one nonzero release identity;\n107\t9. removes the active attempt/slot and makes reuse available only under a fresh identity.\n108\t\n109\tThe account release primitive used here must be non-callback, non-blocking, and incapable of acquiring owner or Manager locks. Account reserve/alias/transfer/release paths that begin while holding `privateB4ByteAccountV2.mu` may mutate account-local state or return, but must never acquire owner or Manager locks; they must instead drop the account lock and re-enter through the Manager-owned operation. Terminal-release losers return false/no-op. They cannot change terminal, release identity, counters, leases, or backing. Required postcondition: no double release, orphan lease, retained byte reference, valid stale alias, or reusable old attempt identity.\n110\t\n111\t## 7. Copy/alias policy\n112\t\n113\t- Owned copy: new retained backing, mandatory prior reservation, exact active lease, one charge.\n114\t- Alias: bounded `(owner_lease_id, offset, length)` view, zero charge, no independent lifetime or publication.\n115\t- Transfer: atomic movement of the complete bytes+lease result, no new charge.\n116\t- Borrow: synchronous bounded use under the owning lease; cannot be stored or returned.\n117\t- Release: exact-once invalidation and lease discharge.\n118\t\n119\tForbidden: reconstruction; remarshal-as-original; digest-as-bytes; capacity inferred after allocation; uncharged retained copy; lease-free byte return; alias escape; hidden scratch retained beyond the operation; publication before reservation; and converting metadata/subledger reservation into a backing owner.\n120\t\n121\t## 8. Concurrency and lock order\n122\t\n123\tThe sole complete order for any nested operation is:\n124\t\n125\t```text\n126\tManager.mu -> callHierarchyLayer1GenericOwner.mu -> privateB4ByteAccountV2.mu\n127\t```\n128\t\n129\tA path may hold a prefix of that order, but never invert or skip backward. In particular:\n130\t\n131\t- owner-held code never acquires `Manager.mu`;\n132\t- account-held code never acquires owner or Manager locks;\n133\t- owner-held code may acquire the account lock only when it already holds Manager lock;\n134\t- account callbacks, waits, retries, or terminal dispatch are forbidden;\n135\t- locks release in reverse order: account, owner, Manager.\n136\t\n137\tNo callbacks, waits, provider operations, allocations, hashing, or external publication run while nested locks are held; only bounded in-memory validation, install/invalidation, account counter mutation, and non-callback lease discharge are allowed. Terminal release uses this complete order and is the only cross-domain discharge coordinator.\n138\t\n139\tRejected alternatives:\n140\t\n141\t1. `privateB4ByteAccountV2.mu -> owner.mu -> Manager.mu`, or any account-held acquisition of owner/Manager: rejected for lock inversion and terminal/reservation deadlock.\n142\t2. `owner.mu -> Manager.mu -> account.mu`: rejected because generic terminal paths already begin at owner and would invert Manager ownership.\n143\t3. release account leases after dropping Manager/owner locks: rejected because a reserve/reuse race could observe cleared backing with undischarged capacity or discharged capacity with valid aliases.\n144\t4. account callback into terminal release: rejected because it creates reverse acquisition and a second terminal coordinator.\n145\t5. try-lock, timeout, goroutine, channel, or deferred asynchronous discharge: rejected because failure becomes schedule-dependent and exact-once release/accounting is no longer atomic.\n146\t6. a second account/owner/terminal solely to avoid nesting: rejected as duplicate custody and authority.\n147\t\n148\tNo new mutex, goroutine, channel, recorder, or terminal is authorized.\n149\t\n150\t## 9. Invariants\n151\t\n152\t```text\n153\tI1  exactly one directional-raw subledger in Manager accounting domain\n154\tI2  exactly one generic backing/terminal owner\n155\tI3  each owned component has one prior exact reservation and corresponding active lease(s)\n156\tI4  each live backing identity has exactly one owning classification\n157\tI5  alias charge = 0 and alias lifetime <= owning lease lifetime\n158\tI6  transfer success preserves exactly one valid owner; failure preserves source only\n159\tI7  sum(component owned capacities) = attempt live bytes = active lease capacity sum\n160\tI8  no reservation/subledger row is itself C15 backing\n161\tI9  every terminal/race converges on one release identity\n162\tI10 every lease releases once; no byte/alias survives release\n163\tI11 incoming and outgoing identities/evidence remain independent\n164\tI12 authority=0, default off, CALLS_ONLY, D/R unchanged\n165\tI13 complete lock order is Manager -> owner -> account; reverse/account-held upward acquisition is impossible\n166\tI14 terminal discharge is atomic across alias invalidation, backing clear, lease release, and account counters\n167\t```\n168\t\n169\tAny invariant violation is a hard stop, not a recoverable fallback.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261005230220-3632 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 private owned-method-pair lease accounting, lifecycle joining, callback drain, refusal atomicity, and compatibility [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006014845-6698 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 marked-custodial retained-notification lease accounting, callback lifetime, lifecycle joining, refusal atomicity, and compatibility. [possibly relevant] [read]\n- 20261006023814-5955 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 marked-custodial unmatched/late retained-response lease accounting, transactional publication, lifecycle joining, and callback non-escape. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261006021001-8737 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 marked-custodial matched ServerError lease accounting, callback lifetime, lifecycle joining, consumer non-escape, and compatibility. [possibly relevant]\n- 20261001214518-6991 — Integration receipt: Independent exact-byte Stage-B T4 completed-STOP lease-retirement RED-to-GREEN implementation/result review [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791903977289},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:06:17.291Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_b1e214c04ebd49b8a4fc7a121e1a0a55|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace48e820b081a2a8d1216c04f57fad","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1\t# Correction-safe C15 enumeration plan over current source\n2\t\n3\tStatus: `PLANNED_NOT_ENUMERATED`. No final count or disposition is claimed.\n4\t\n5\t## Scope and baseline\n6\t\n7\tSource pin is HEAD `162d796f7e33fea2c2bdb98f92e41744bb728c2d`; exact files and hashes are in `SOURCE_MANIFEST.sha256`. The historical 54-seam census is baseline evidence only. The mechanical run must first identify every prior uncharged relationship relevant to prepare frame, prepare result, selected handoff, directional frame, directional result, and retained external/evidence custody. A historical row is not automatically current or accepted.\n8\t\n9\tCandidate discovery searches current source for allocations, copies, appends, frame/result captures, byte slices retained across calls, publications, owner fields, lease creation/release, alias/view/span construction, transfer/move/invalidation, callbacks, terminal paths, and generated C15 registry entries. Source locators nominate rows; they do not adjudicate ownership.\n10\t\n11\t## Required finite outputs\n12\t\n13\tProduce exact deterministic TSVs:\n14\t\n15\t- `BASELINE_PRIOR_UNCHARGED.tsv`\n16\t- `ADDED.tsv`\n17\t- `CHANGED.tsv`\n18\t- `REMOVED.tsv`\n19\t- `UNCHANGED.tsv`\n20\t- `ALLOCATION_SITES.tsv`\n21\t- `RELEASE_SITES.tsv`\n22\t- `BORROW_ALIAS_SITES.tsv`\n23\t- `TRANSFER_SITES.tsv`\n24\t- `SOURCE_LOCATIONS.tsv`\n25\t- `UNRESOLVED.tsv`\n26\t- `COUNTS.json`\n27\t- `RUN_MANIFEST.sha256`\n28\t\n29\tExpected meaning, not expected count:\n30\t\n31\t| Delta | Meaning |\n32\t|---|---|\n33\t| `ADDED` | current/new governed relationship absent from accepted baseline |\n34\t| `CHANGED` | same stable row identity, changed source/class/lifecycle/lease semantics |\n35\t| `REMOVED` | baseline relationship absent at current source with exact deletion evidence |\n36\t| `UNCHANGED` | same identity and adjudicated semantics at exact current source |\n37\t\n38\tAll four sets are exhaustive, pairwise disjoint, and their union equals baseline plus current candidate identities under the declared reconciliation equation. No actual counts are frozen here. Any produced counts are labeled `PROVISIONAL_MECHANICAL` until independent adjudication.\n39\t\n40\t## Mechanical row schema\n41\t\n42\tEach row has exactly these fields:\n43\t\n44\t```text\n45\trow_id\n46\trevision\n47\tpredecessor_row_id\n48\tpredecessor_revision\n49\tstatus\n50\tsource_path\n51\tsource_start_line\n52\tsource_end_line\n53\tsource_sha256\n54\tsymbol\n55\toperation_kind = ALLOCATE|COPY|RETAIN|ALIAS|BORROW|TRANSFER|RELEASE|PUBLISH\n56\tcomponent = PREPARE_FRAME|PREPARE_RESULT|SELECTED_HANDOFF|DIRECTIONAL_FRAME|DIRECTIONAL_RESULT|RETAINED_EXTERNAL_EVIDENCE\n57\tattempt_scope\n58\taccount_scope\n59\tbacking_identity_rule\n60\tsource_lease_identity_rule\n61\tdestination_lease_identity_rule\n62\tcapacity_rule\n63\treservation_site\n64\tallocation_site\n65\trelease_site\n66\tborrow_alias_site\n67\ttransfer_site\n68\tterminal_paths\n69\tbaseline_row_id\n70\tdelta = ADDED|CHANGED|REMOVED|UNCHANGED\n71\tprovisional_class = GOVERNED_OWNER|ZERO_CHARGE_ALIAS|SEPARATELY_CHARGED_COPY|ATOMIC_TRANSFER|POLICY_BLOCKED|TEST_ONLY_EXCLUSION|OPAQUE_SCRATCH_EXCLUSION|UNRESOLVED\n72\tcontrary_evidence\n73\trejection_condition\n74\tauthority_ceiling\n75\tadjudicator_id\n76\tadjudication_revision\n77\tnotes\n78\t```\n79\t\n80\t`row_id = sha256(\"adr0011.c15.lease-source.v2.row\\x00\" || source_path || \"\\x00\" || symbol || \"\\x00\" || operation_kind || \"\\x00\" || component || \"\\x00\" || backing_identity_rule)`. This is the stable logical identity and therefore remains constant across revisions of one relationship. The canonical revision-record hash is `sha256(\"adr0011.c15.lease-source.v2.revision\\x00\" || row_id || \"\\x00\" || uint64be(revision) || \"\\x00\" || predecessor_row_id || \"\\x00\" || uint64be(predecessor_revision) || \"\\x00\" || canonical_tsv_row_without_record_hash)`, and is emitted in the run manifest. Paths use repository-relative slash form; symbols are fully qualified package-local names; no line number enters identity, so line movement alone does not create false add/remove. Ambiguous identities become separate `UNRESOLVED` candidates rather than guessed merges.\n81\t\n82\t## Exact correction lineage\n83\t\n84\tThe genesis sentinel is exact: `predecessor_row_id=NULL` and `predecessor_revision=0`. It is valid only for `revision=1`. For every later revision, `predecessor_row_id` must equal `row_id`, `predecessor_revision` must equal `revision-1`, and `revision` must increase by exactly one. A correction never overwrites or deletes its predecessor.\n85\t\n86\tValidation builds a graph keyed by `(row_id, revision)` and requires:\n87\t\n88\t- exactly one genesis and exactly one current tip per `row_id`;\n89\t- every non-genesis predecessor exists in the same frozen run/evidence closure and its record hash verifies;\n90\t- no cycle, self-loop, skipped revision, duplicate revision, missing predecessor, or decreasing revision;\n91\t- no branching: more than one record naming the same predecessor is `UNRESOLVED`, not an automatic merge;\n92\t- no cross-row predecessor except an explicit split/merge adjudication record; split/merge creates new genesis row IDs whose notes name all source tips, while source tips receive their own next revision marking the finite delta;\n93\t- `ADDED` begins at genesis; `CHANGED`, `REMOVED`, and corrected `UNCHANGED` revisions follow the same row chain; a removed row remains a terminal historical tip and cannot be silently resurrected—reintroduction uses a new row identity or an independently adjudicated correction explaining continuity.\n94\t\n95\tCycle, missing predecessor, branch, ambiguous split/merge, or hash mismatch creates an `UNRESOLVED` row and blocks GO. Independent adjudication verifies both semantic disposition and lineage topology; the mechanical producer cannot adjudicate its own branch resolution.\n96\t\n97\t## Exact source manifest rule\n98\t\n99\t`SOURCE_MANIFEST.sha256` is the input manifest and includes every six-production current source/dependency, the absent required-new production path, all four absent required-new test paths, historical C15 baseline, generic amendment, immutable v1/v2 interfaces, and frozen write-set package. Before enumeration, regenerate it from the exact HEAD and require byte equality. Any drift stops this package and requires a new version.\n100\t\n101\tGenerated outputs include their tool/script bytes, argv, environment-affecting values, stdout/stderr, exit status, and hashes. Run twice from identical pins and require byte-identical outputs.\n102\t\n103\t## Reconciliation and lifecycle checks\n104\t\n105\tFor every current candidate:\n106\t\n107\t1. identify exact allocation/copy/retention or prove alias/borrow;\n108\t2. identify reservation and exact charged capacity before effect;\n109\t3. identify owning account/attempt/component and lease source;\n110\t4. identify every borrow/alias bound and no-escape rule;\n111\t5. identify atomic transfer source/destination and failure preservation;\n112\t6. identify every normal/error/refusal/cancel/timeout/STOP/RESTART/Shutdown/race release path;\n113\t7. prove one release winner, no double release, no orphan lease, no retained bytes after release;\n114\t8. join to exactly one delta row;\n115\t9. validate the complete predecessor chain and canonical revision-record hash.\n116\t\n117\tRequired equations:\n118\t\n119\t```text\n120\tbaseline identities = CHANGED + REMOVED + baseline-side UNCHANGED\n121\tcurrent identities  = ADDED + CHANGED + current-side UNCHANGED\n122\tall current candidates = allocation/copy + zero-charge alias/borrow + transfer/release operation rows\n123\towned live capacity = exact sum(active corresponding lease capacities)\n124\tfor each row_id: revisions = contiguous 1..tip and predecessor(r) = (row_id, r-1)\n125\tlineage roots = exact (NULL, 0) genesis sentinels\n126\tlineage cycles + missing predecessors + unresolved branches = 0\n127\tUNRESOLVED count = 0 before GO\n128\t```\n129\t\n130\t## Independent adjudication\n131\t\n132\tA separate review pass, identified in each row by `adjudicator_id` and `adjudication_revision`, reviews source bytes without inheriting mechanical classifications. It challenges hidden copies, alias escape, lease mismatch, transfer partiality, release gaps, row merges/splits, transitive assumptions, baseline carry-forward, and bounded-zero/absence claims. Independence is a review relationship; no delegation is required.\n133\t\n134\tEvery non-`UNRESOLVED` row requires contrary evidence or a falsifier. Corrections create a new monotonically increasing row revision with exact `predecessor_row_id` and `predecessor_revision`, verified canonical revision hash, and finite delta; native source evidence is never rewritten. The independent pass rejects cycles, missing predecessors, branches, duplicate tips, and unjustified split/merge continuity or leaves them `UNRESOLVED`. Structural adjacency, names, CALLS, or generated registry membership cannot accept identity.\n135\t\n136\tGate prerequisites:\n137\t\n138\t- both deterministic mechanical runs match;\n139\t- all manifests/checksums verify;\n140\t- every source candidate and baseline identity reconciles;\n141\t- every allocation/release/borrow/transfer site is adjudicated;\n142\t- `UNRESOLVED.tsv` exists with header only and `UNRESOLVED=0` in counts;\n143\t- no write-set expansion or architecture hard stop;\n144\t- independent reviewer returns the exact gate for this package checksum.\n145\t\n146\tUntil then disposition remains `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20260821193348-8201 — Current-source access orientation selects a six-repository predecessor-impact envelope [possibly relevant]\n- 20260824234609-5129 — Five current-source observations renew three ScopeRationalization rows at evidence tier only [possibly relevant]\n- 20260814163906-4069 — The retained EASI guide does not define row-count, checksum, semantic, or rollback acceptance checks. [possibly relevant]\n- 20260827162246-6425 — Post-exact24 orientation selects independent exact-two blocked-row source recovery [possibly relevant]\n- 20260826200941-1958 — Post-row-21 completion orientation selects row-1 metadata candidate-gap adjudication [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791903977290},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:06:17.291Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
{"isSidechain":true,"agentId":"73ef3d2e-c865-43f","type":"toolResult","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_1ddae0885bef4ee6a6bdaf9db7e1e474|fc_07dc770452ad3266016ace48e820b081a2aa47fc07feb0c9a8","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1\t# Exact immutable future write-set\n2\t\n3\tStatus: `AUTHORED_NOT_GO`. This package changes none of these production/test files.\n4\t\n5\t## Production: exactly six\n6\t\n7\t1. `sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_private.go` — required-new private mechanics; successor lease-bearing acquisition/account/alias/transfer declarations.\n8\t2. `sessionruntime/sessionruntime.go` — one Manager subledger; reserve-before-effect integration and terminal convergence under existing lock.\n9\t3. `internal/lspwire/read_frame.go` — private bounded acquisition result carrying bytes with corresponding lease source; defaults unchanged.\n10\t4. `internal/lspwire/successor_ingress.go` — conditional already-reserved bound and acquisition threading only; byte-identical if unused.\n11\t5. `sessionruntime/b4_owned_method_pair_lease.go` — sole direction-neutral owner/terminal integration, atomic acquisition transfer, alias invalidation, exact release.\n12\t6. `sessionruntime/b4_c15_ownership_registry_private.go` — generated only from accepted `UNRESOLVED=0` enumeration; never hand-edited.\n13\t\n14\t## Tests: exactly four new files\n15\t\n16\t1. `sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_private_test.go`.\n17\t2. `sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_race_private_test.go`.\n18\t3. `internal/lspwire/read_frame_bounded_incomplete_v1_private_test.go`.\n19\t4. `internal/lspwire/successor_ingress_directional_v1_private_test.go`.\n20\t\n21\tThe existing selector/package ownership remains unchanged. Future tests must additionally prove every component reservation tuple, lease-bearing no-escape acquisition, zero-charge alias lifetime, atomic bytes+lease transfer in both success/failure, every terminal/race release convergence, no double/orphan, and exact C15 delta reconciliation.\n22\t\n23\tWithout adding files, `sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_race_private_test.go` owns planned adversarial schedules for terminal release versus account reserve, alias declaration/use, acquisition transfer, and ordinary account/lease release. Each schedule must prove the only nested order is `Manager.mu -> callHierarchyLayer1GenericOwner.mu -> privateB4ByteAccountV2.mu`, account-held paths never acquire owner/Manager, one terminal winner, bounded completion without deadlock/livelock, exact counter/lease/alias postconditions, and duplicate losers as no-op. `sessionruntime/call_hierarchy_directional_raw_v1_private_test.go` owns deterministic lock-contract/refusal and terminal-discharge postconditions. The two existing `internal/lspwire` test files remain transport-only and must not fabricate account locking. These are planned obligations only; no test is created or run here.\n24\t\n25\t## Hard stop\n26\t\n27\tThere is no fallback or expansion. If any architecture, interface, RED, implementation, enumeration, generation, compatibility, or release obligation requires an unlisted production/test path, historical test/fixture/corpus/golden mutation, public surface, dependency, schema/profile/registry/config/build-tag/package-boundary change, the exact disposition is:\n28\t\n29\t`BLOCKED_WRITESET_EXPANSION_REQUIRED`\n30\t\n31\tNo implementation or test mutation may proceed under this package.\n\n## Related notes\n- 20261006235523-4470 — Integration receipt: Independent read-only DESIGN_GO review of ADR0011 C18 owner and write-set proposal [possibly relevant]\n- 20261010201159-8643 — Integration receipt: Author, correct, and independently review incoming Go/gopls CALLS qualification plan [possibly relevant]\n- 20261005230220-3632 — Integration receipt: Independently review ADR0011 C15 private owned-method-pair lease accounting, lifecycle joining, callback drain, refusal atomicity, and compatibility [possibly relevant]\n- 20261004222557-4857 — Integration receipt: Independent read-only integration review of ADR0011 C15 private-B4 returned request-frame ownership via bounded caller lease [possibly relevant]\n- 20260725001014-8818 — The NAIS pitch committed to phased dual-running migration under NAIS go-no-go authority [possibly relevant]\nResolve each unread related note — run `nn show <id>` to open, or write `skip-related: <id> [<id> ...] — <reason>` to dismiss. Notes marked [read] have already been loaded this session and do not require action.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1791903977290},"timestamp":"2026-10-13T15:06:17.291Z","cwd":"/Users/schwa/dev/lsp-trace"}
